window.CLF_EXAMS=window.CLF_EXAMS||[];
window.CLF_EXAMS.push({"id":10,"qs":[{"id":"E1A-46","d":1,"ts":"1.1.7","t":"Lambda partial batch response","q":"A Lambda function processes batches of 500 records from an Amazon Kinesis data stream. Occasionally, a few records in a batch fail because of a downstream validation error. Today, any failure causes the entire batch to be retried, so successful records are processed again and create duplicates. How should the data engineer change the configuration so that only the failed records and the records after them are retried?","o":["Enable ReportBatchItemFailures on the event source mapping and have the function return the sequence number of the first failed record in batchItemFailures.","Set the batch size to 1 record.","Enable BisectBatchOnFunctionError and keep returning an error for the whole batch.","Set MaximumRetryAttempts to 0."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: hanya 'a few records' yang gagal, dan retry seluruh batch menyebabkan 'duplicates'. Dengan function response type ReportBatchItemFailures, fungsi mengembalikan daftar batchItemFailures berisi sequence number record yang gagal; Lambda lalu melakukan checkpoint pada record sukses sebelumnya dan me-retry mulai dari record gagal tersebut, sehingga record yang sudah sukses tidak diproses ulang. Distraktor terdekat adalah BisectBatchOnFunctionError: membagi batch, tetapi record yang sudah sukses di separuh batch yang gagal tetap bisa diproses ulang. Batch size 1 menghilangkan masalah tetapi sangat menurunkan throughput dan menaikkan biaya. MaximumRetryAttempts 0 membuang record gagal tanpa retry. Aturan umum: partial batch failure di Kinesis/DynamoDB Streams/SQS = ReportBatchItemFailures; tetap rancang consumer idempotent.","r":["Benar — Partial batch response membuat Lambda me-retry mulai dari record yang gagal, bukan seluruh batch.","Salah — Batch size 1 menurunkan throughput secara drastis dan menaikkan biaya.","Salah — Bisect masih dapat memproses ulang record sukses di separuh batch yang gagal.","Salah — Record yang gagal tidak di-retry sama sekali sehingga data hilang."],"k":"Retry hanya record yang gagal → ReportBatchItemFailures (partial batch response)."},{"id":"E1B-23","d":1,"ts":"1.2.2","t":"Parallel JDBC reads in AWS Glue","q":"An AWS Glue ETL job reads a 500-million-row table from Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL through a JDBC connection. The job uses 20 G.1X workers, but the Spark UI shows that only a single task reads from the database and the read phase takes several hours. Which change will improve read performance the MOST?","o":["Increase the number of workers from 20 to 60.","Configure the JDBC source with a hashfield or hashexpression and a hashpartitions value so that Glue reads the table in parallel.","Change the worker type from G.1X to G.8X.","Enable job bookmarks on the JDBC source."],"a":[1],"e":"Gejala kuncinya adalah 'only a single task reads from the database' walaupun ada 20 worker. Secara default, pembacaan JDBC terjadi melalui satu koneksi sehingga hanya satu task yang bekerja, apa pun jumlah worker-nya. Dengan opsi hashfield/hashexpression dan hashpartitions, Glue membagi query menjadi beberapa partisi yang dibaca paralel oleh banyak task. Menambah worker atau memakai G.8X adalah distraktor yang menggoda, tetapi keduanya tidak mengubah fakta bahwa hanya satu koneksi yang membaca data. Job bookmark hanya membatasi data ke baris baru untuk run berikutnya dan tidak memparalelkan pembacaan awal. Aturan umum: pembacaan JDBC lambat dengan satu task → aktifkan parallel read (hashpartitions di Glue, atau partitionColumn/numPartitions di Spark).","r":["Salah — Worker tambahan menganggur karena pembacaan JDBC tetap hanya satu task.","Benar — hashfield/hashexpression + hashpartitions membagi pembacaan menjadi beberapa query paralel.","Salah — Worker lebih besar tidak menambah paralelisme pembacaan JDBC.","Salah — Bookmark mengatur pemrosesan inkremental, bukan paralelisme pembacaan."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'JDBC read uses one task / slow' → parallel reads (hashpartitions/hashfield di Glue; partitionColumn di Spark)."},{"id":"E3A-12","d":3,"ts":"3.1.4","t":"AWS Glue job bookmarks","q":"An AWS Glue Spark job runs every night and processes CSV files from an Amazon S3 prefix where new files are added daily. Each run reads all historical files again, so the runtime and cost keep growing. The job should process only files that were added since the last successful run, with the LEAST development effort. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Add custom code that stores the last processed timestamp in Amazon DynamoDB and filters files by timestamp.","Enable job bookmarks for the Glue job and use a transformation_ctx for the source in the script.","Move processed files to an archive prefix with an AWS Lambda function after every run.","Run an AWS Glue crawler before each job run so that the job reads only new partitions."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'process only files that were added since the last successful run' dan 'LEAST development effort'. Glue job bookmarks menyimpan state data yang sudah diproses, sehingga run berikutnya hanya membaca file baru dari S3. Cukup aktifkan job bookmark di konfigurasi job dan pastikan sumber data memakai parameter transformation_ctx (serta job.commit() di akhir script). Menyimpan timestamp sendiri di DynamoDB berfungsi, tetapi Anda menulis dan merawat logika yang sudah disediakan Glue. Memindahkan file dengan Lambda menambah komponen dan risiko kehilangan data jika job gagal di tengah. Crawler hanya memperbarui metadata Data Catalog; ia tidak membuat job membaca data baru saja. Aturan umum: 'incremental processing' di Glue → job bookmarks.","r":["Salah — Berfungsi, tetapi membangun ulang fitur yang sudah ada di Glue sehingga upaya pengembangan lebih besar.","Benar — Job bookmarks melacak data yang sudah diproses sehingga setiap run hanya membaca file baru.","Salah — Menambah komponen Lambda dan berisiko tidak sinkron dengan status job.","Salah — Crawler hanya memperbarui metadata, bukan membatasi data yang dibaca job."],"k":"Tips ujian: Glue 'process only new data' → job bookmarks."},{"id":"E1C-72","d":1,"ts":"1.4.9","t":"CodePipeline for data pipelines","q":"A data engineering team keeps AWS Glue job scripts and CloudFormation templates in a GitHub repository. On every merge to main, the team wants to automatically run unit tests, deploy to a staging account, wait for a manual approval from the data lead, and then deploy to production. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Run a Jenkins server on Amazon EC2 that polls the repository and runs deployment scripts.","Use an AWS CodePipeline pipeline with a GitHub source through an AWS CodeConnections connection, an AWS CodeBuild stage for tests, a CloudFormation deploy action to staging, a manual approval action, and a CloudFormation deploy action to production.","Ask each engineer to run the tests locally and deploy with the AWS CLI after merging.","Use an Amazon EventBridge rule on the GitHub repository to start a Lambda function that deploys directly to production."],"a":[1],"e":"Kebutuhannya: otomatis 'on every merge to main', menjalankan 'unit tests', deploy ke staging, menunggu 'manual approval', lalu produksi, dengan 'LEAST operational overhead'. AWS CodePipeline adalah layanan CI/CD terkelola yang menyusun stage: source dari GitHub melalui CodeConnections, build/test dengan CodeBuild, deploy dengan action CloudFormation, dan manual approval action yang menghentikan pipeline sampai disetujui. Distractor terdekat adalah Jenkins di EC2: dapat memenuhi alur yang sama, tetapi server, plugin, dan patching harus dikelola sendiri. Proses manual tidak konsisten dan tidak otomatis. EventBridge ke Lambda langsung ke produksi melewatkan tes, staging, dan approval. Aturan umum: CI/CD terkelola di AWS → CodePipeline + CodeBuild (+ CloudFormation/CodeDeploy) dengan manual approval untuk gerbang produksi.","r":["Salah — Server Jenkins menambah overhead pengelolaan.","Benar — CodePipeline menyusun source, test, deploy staging, approval, dan deploy produksi secara terkelola.","Salah — Proses manual tidak otomatis dan rawan kesalahan.","Salah — Melewatkan tes, staging, dan approval."],"k":"Tips ujian: CI/CD + 'manual approval before prod' → CodePipeline + CodeBuild + approval action."},{"id":"E1A-69","d":1,"ts":"1.1.12","t":"Lambda tumbling windows","q":"A data engineer needs to compute simple per-device totals over consecutive, non-overlapping 1-minute intervals from an Amazon Kinesis data stream. The team prefers to keep using AWS Lambda and does not want to introduce an external state store or a new service. Which approach meets these requirements?","o":["Store the totals in the /tmp directory of the Lambda function.","Configure a tumbling window on the Lambda event source mapping and return the running state from each invocation so that Lambda passes it to the next invocation in the window.","Enable enhanced fan-out on the stream.","Set the event source mapping batch size to 1 so that each record is processed independently."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: agregasi 'non-overlapping 1-minute intervals' (tumbling window), tetap memakai 'AWS Lambda', tanpa 'external state store'. Lambda untuk Kinesis dan DynamoDB Streams mendukung tumbling windows (hingga 15 menit): fungsi mengembalikan state, dan Lambda meneruskan state itu ke invocation berikutnya dalam window yang sama, lalu menandai akhir window sehingga fungsi dapat mengeluarkan hasil akhir. State ini dikelola per shard. Distraktor terdekat adalah menyimpan di /tmp: penyimpanan itu lokal per execution environment, tidak dijamin bertahan dan tidak dibagi antar-environment. Enhanced fan-out dan batch size 1 tidak menyediakan state. Aturan umum: Lambda pada dasarnya stateless; agregasi sederhana berbasis waktu = tumbling window Lambda, sedangkan state kompleks atau sliding window = Flink.","r":["Salah — /tmp bersifat lokal per execution environment dan tidak andal untuk state agregasi.","Benar — Tumbling window Lambda meneruskan state antar-invocation dalam window tanpa layanan tambahan.","Salah — Enhanced fan-out menambah throughput baca, tidak menyediakan state.","Salah — Memproses per record tidak memberi agregasi dan menurunkan throughput."],"k":"Agregasi sederhana non-overlapping di Lambda (Kinesis/DynamoDB Streams) → tumbling window (≤ 15 menit)."},{"id":"E4A-25","d":4,"ts":"4.1.7","t":"SageMaker Unified Studio domain units","q":"A company uses one Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio domain for the whole enterprise. The finance and marketing business units each want to decide which of their own users can create projects, without asking the central domain administrators every time, while still sharing assets through the same business catalog. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Create a separate AWS account and a separate SageMaker Unified Studio domain for each business unit.","Create IAM groups for each business unit and attach a policy that allows all datazone actions.","Create a domain unit for each business unit, assign business unit leads as domain unit owners, and let them manage the project creation policy for their domain unit.","Use AWS Lake Formation LF-Tags to tag each business unit's tables and grant project creation through the tags."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'decide which of their own users can create projects' dan 'still sharing assets through the same business catalog'. Di SageMaker Unified Studio, domain unit dipakai untuk mengorganisasi asset dan entitas domain per unit bisnis atau tim. Domain unit owner menerima wewenang yang didelegasikan, dan di dalam domain unit dapat ditetapkan authorization policy seperti project creation policy dan project membership policy untuk user dan grup. Dengan begitu tiap unit bisnis mengelola sendiri siapa yang boleh membuat project, tetapi semua tetap berada di satu domain dan satu business catalog. Domain terpisah per unit bisnis memecah catalog dan menambah overhead. IAM policy datazone:* terlalu luas dan tidak memodelkan delegasi per unit bisnis. LF-Tags mengatur akses ke data di Data Catalog, bukan pembuatan project. Aturan umum: struktur organisasi + delegasi wewenang di dalam satu domain → domain units dan authorization policies.","r":["Salah — Domain terpisah memecah business catalog dan menambah overhead administrasi.","Salah — Policy datazone:* terlalu luas dan tidak memberi delegasi per unit bisnis.","Benar — Domain unit dengan owner dan project creation policy mendelegasikan kontrol ke unit bisnis dalam satu domain bersama.","Salah — LF-Tags mengatur izin data di Lake Formation, bukan siapa yang boleh membuat project."],"k":"Tips ujian: delegasi per unit bisnis di SageMaker Unified Studio → domain units + authorization policies (project creation policy)."},{"id":"E2A-34","d":2,"ts":"2.1.4","t":"Transfer Family AS2","q":"A manufacturer exchanges purchase orders and invoices with large retail partners. The retail partners require the Applicability Statement 2 (AS2) protocol with signed and encrypted messages and message disposition notifications (MDNs). Received documents must be stored in Amazon S3 for an ETL pipeline. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Deploy an open source AS2 server on Amazon ECS and write received messages to Amazon S3.","Create an AWS Transfer Family SFTP server and ask partners to switch to SFTP.","Use Amazon API Gateway with an AWS Lambda function to receive and decrypt AS2 messages.","Use AWS Transfer Family with the AS2 protocol and an Amazon S3 storage location."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci adalah partner yang 'require the Applicability Statement 2 (AS2) protocol' dengan signing, enkripsi, dan MDN, serta 'LEAST operational overhead'. AWS Transfer Family mendukung AS2 secara native, termasuk penandatanganan, enkripsi, dan pengiriman MDN, serta menyimpan pesan yang diterima ke S3 untuk diproses pipeline ETL. Distraktor terdekat adalah server AS2 open source di ECS: memenuhi protokol, tetapi tim harus mengelola container, sertifikat, dan kepatuhan protokol. Meminta partner beralih ke SFTP melanggar persyaratan mereka. API Gateway + Lambda berarti mengimplementasikan protokol AS2 sendiri, yang rumit. Aturan umum: B2B/EDI dengan AS2 → AWS Transfer Family AS2.","r":["Salah — Server AS2 self-managed di ECS menambah beban operasional dan pengelolaan sertifikat.","Salah — Partner mewajibkan AS2; SFTP tidak memenuhi persyaratan protokol mereka.","Salah — Mengimplementasikan AS2 (signing, enkripsi, MDN) secara kustom di Lambda rumit dan rawan kesalahan.","Benar — Transfer Family mendukung AS2 secara managed dan menyimpan dokumen ke S3 untuk pipeline ETL."],"k":"AS2 / EDI B2B exchange → AWS Transfer Family AS2."},{"id":"E2A-23","d":2,"ts":"2.1.3","t":"Purpose-built databases: Neptune","q":"A bank wants to detect fraud rings by analyzing relationships between accounts, devices, phone numbers, and IP addresses. Investigators need to run queries that traverse 4 to 6 levels of connections in milliseconds, for example finding all accounts that share a device with an account that shares a phone number with a flagged account. Which data store is MOST appropriate?","o":["Amazon Neptune","Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL with recursive self-joins","Amazon Redshift","Amazon DynamoDB with adjacency list design"],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'relationships', 'traverse 4 to 6 levels of connections', dan 'in milliseconds'. Amazon Neptune adalah graph database fully managed yang menyimpan node dan edge secara native dan mendukung bahasa query graph seperti Gremlin, openCypher, dan SPARQL, sehingga traversal multi-hop tetap cepat. Distraktor terdekat adalah RDS PostgreSQL dengan recursive join: secara teknis mungkin, tetapi setiap level menambah join mahal sehingga performa menurun drastis pada kedalaman 4–6. DynamoDB adjacency list cocok untuk relasi sederhana satu-dua hop, bukan traversal dalam yang ad-hoc. Redshift ditujukan untuk agregasi analitik, bukan traversal relasi latensi rendah. Aturan umum: relasi yang sangat terhubung dan traversal multi-hop (fraud ring, social network, knowledge graph) → Amazon Neptune.","r":["Benar — Neptune menyimpan data sebagai graph dan menjalankan traversal multi-hop dengan latensi rendah.","Salah — Recursive join pada database relasional menjadi lambat dan kompleks saat kedalaman relasi bertambah.","Salah — Redshift adalah data warehouse untuk agregasi, bukan traversal graph latensi milidetik.","Salah — Adjacency list di DynamoDB membutuhkan banyak query berurutan untuk traversal dalam dan sulit untuk query ad-hoc."],"k":"Highly connected data + multi-hop traversal → Amazon Neptune."},{"id":"E2B-60","d":2,"ts":"2.3.6","t":"Aurora high availability and DR","q":"A company stores its operational data in Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL, and nightly AWS Glue jobs extract the data to the data lake. The company requires automatic failover within the Region if an Availability Zone fails, and the ability to recover in another Region with an RPO of about 1 second if the primary Region fails. Which TWO actions meet these requirements? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Add at least one Aurora Replica in a different Availability Zone of the same DB cluster.","Take manual DB cluster snapshots every hour and copy them to the second Region.","Convert the cluster to an Aurora global database with a secondary DB cluster in the second Region.","Create an RDS read replica of the cluster on an Amazon EC2 instance in the second Region.","Enable AWS Backup daily backups with a cross-Region copy rule."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'automatic failover within the Region if an Availability Zone fails' dan 'another Region with an RPO of about 1 second'. Di Aurora, storage sudah direplikasi ke tiga AZ, tetapi failover otomatis compute membutuhkan Aurora Replica di AZ lain yang bisa dipromosikan menjadi writer. Untuk DR lintas Region, Aurora Global Database mereplikasi data ke cluster sekunder di Region lain dengan lag replikasi yang biasanya di bawah 1 detik, sehingga RPO sekitar 1 detik tercapai dan cluster sekunder bisa dipromosikan. Snapshot per jam dan AWS Backup harian memberi RPO jam hingga hari. Read replica di EC2 bukan opsi yang ada untuk Aurora. Ingat: HA dalam Region → Aurora Replica di AZ lain; DR lintas Region dengan RPO detik → Aurora Global Database.","r":["Benar — Aurora Replica di AZ lain memungkinkan failover otomatis saat AZ writer gagal.","Salah — Snapshot per jam memberi RPO hingga satu jam, jauh dari target 1 detik.","Benar — Aurora Global Database memberi replikasi lintas Region dengan lag biasanya di bawah 1 detik.","Salah — Read replica Aurora tidak dibuat di EC2, dan ini bukan pola DR yang didukung.","Salah — Backup harian memberi RPO hingga 24 jam."],"k":"Tips ujian: Aurora 'AZ failover' → Aurora Replica di AZ lain; 'cross-Region RPO ~1s' → Aurora Global Database."},{"id":"E2C-11","d":2,"ts":"2.4.2","t":"Glue crawler schema change handling for partitions","q":"A data engineer uses an AWS Glue crawler to catalog daily CSV partitions in Amazon S3 (s3://bucket/sales/dt=YYYY-MM-DD/). The source system recently added two columns at the end of the file. The crawler updated the table schema, but Amazon Athena queries that span old and new partitions now fail with HIVE_PARTITION_SCHEMA_MISMATCH. Which action resolves the issue with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Delete the table and all partitions and re-run the crawler from scratch every day.","Configure the crawler option to update all new and existing partitions with metadata from the table, and re-run the crawler.","Rewrite all historical CSV files with an AWS Glue job so that they contain the two new columns.","Create a separate Athena table for the files written after the schema change and use UNION ALL in every query."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah error HIVE_PARTITION_SCHEMA_MISMATCH setelah kolom baru ditambahkan, dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Error ini terjadi karena setiap partisi di Glue Data Catalog menyimpan schema-nya sendiri, sehingga partisi lama dan baru memiliki definisi kolom yang berbeda dari tabel. Opsi crawler 'Update all new and existing partitions with metadata from the table' (partition inherit dari tabel) membuat semua partisi memakai schema tabel, sehingga Athena dapat membaca partisi lama (kolom baru bernilai NULL) dan partisi baru. Menghapus dan membuat ulang tabel setiap hari berisiko dan tetap tidak menyelaraskan schema per partisi secara permanen. Menulis ulang semua file historis mahal dan tidak perlu. Membuat dua tabel dengan UNION ALL menambah kompleksitas query untuk semua pengguna. Aturan umum: schema partisi tidak cocok dengan tabel → setel crawler agar partisi mewarisi schema tabel.","r":["Salah — Menghapus dan membuat ulang tabel setiap hari berisiko mengganggu konsumen dan tidak menyelesaikan akar masalah secara rapi.","Benar — Partisi mewarisi schema tabel sehingga partisi lama dan baru konsisten dan Athena tidak lagi error.","Salah — Menulis ulang seluruh data historis mahal dan tidak perlu karena kolom baru di akhir file dapat dibaca sebagai NULL.","Salah — Dua tabel dengan UNION ALL di setiap query menambah kompleksitas dan beban bagi analis."],"k":"Tips ujian: HIVE_PARTITION_SCHEMA_MISMATCH → crawler 'update all new and existing partitions with metadata from the table'."},{"id":"E3B-70","d":3,"ts":"3.4.5","t":"DynamoDB write sharding","q":"A gaming company stores player events in an Amazon DynamoDB table with event_date as the partition key. All writes for the current day go to the same partition key value, causing throttling even though the table has plenty of provisioned write capacity overall. Which design change will distribute the writes MOST evenly?","o":["Switch the table to on-demand capacity mode and keep the same key design.","Add a global secondary index on event_date.","Enable DynamoDB Streams on the table.","Use write sharding by appending a random or calculated suffix (for example, event_date#1 to event_date#20) to the partition key, and query all suffixes when reading a day."],"a":[3],"e":"Gejala kuncinya: semua tulisan hari ini masuk ke 'same partition key value' sehingga terjadi throttling walaupun kapasitas total tabel cukup — ini skew tulis (hot partition). Write sharding menambahkan suffix acak atau terhitung pada partition key sehingga tulisan untuk satu hari tersebar ke banyak partisi fisik; saat membaca, aplikasi melakukan query ke semua suffix dan menggabungkan hasilnya. Distraktor terdekat adalah on-demand mode: mempermudah kapasitas tetapi batas throughput per partition key tetap berlaku, sehingga satu kunci panas masih bisa throttled. GSI dengan kunci yang sama mewarisi masalah hot key dan dapat menyebabkan throttling balik ke tabel. Streams hanya menangkap perubahan. Aturan: hot partition DynamoDB → kunci berkardinalitas tinggi atau write sharding.","r":["Salah — Mode on-demand tidak menghapus batas throughput per partisi untuk satu kunci panas.","Salah — GSI pada event_date memiliki kunci panas yang sama dan bisa ikut throttled.","Salah — Streams menangkap perubahan data dan tidak menyebarkan beban tulis.","Benar — Suffix pada partition key menyebarkan tulisan satu hari ke banyak partisi."],"k":"Tips ujian: DynamoDB hot partition (tanggal/status sebagai PK) → write sharding dengan suffix."},{"id":"E1C-25","d":1,"ts":"1.3.3","t":"Step Functions Express vs Standard","q":"A company receives about 50,000 clickstream events per second through an API. Each event must go through a short workflow of validation, enrichment, and a write to Amazon DynamoDB that completes in under 2 seconds. Occasional duplicate processing is acceptable because the DynamoDB write is idempotent. The company wants to orchestrate this with AWS Step Functions at the LOWEST cost. Which workflow type should the data engineer use?","o":["Standard workflows, because they provide exactly-once execution.","Express workflows, because they support very high event rates, short durations, and are priced by number and duration of executions.","Standard workflows with an Inline Map state to batch events.","Express workflows with a .waitForTaskToken callback task for each event."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya '50,000 events per second', 'under 2 seconds', 'duplicate processing is acceptable', dan 'LOWEST cost'. Express workflows dirancang untuk beban volume tinggi dan berdurasi pendek (maksimum 5 menit), dengan harga berdasarkan jumlah eksekusi, durasi, dan memori, sehingga jauh lebih murah daripada Standard yang dihitung per state transition. Semantik at-least-once pada Express asinkron dapat diterima karena penulisan DynamoDB bersifat idempotent. Distractor terdekat adalah Standard workflow: exactly-once tidak dibutuhkan di sini, sementara biaya per transition dan kuota laju StartExecution tidak cocok untuk puluhan ribu event per detik. Callback task token tidak didukung pada Express workflows. Aturan umum: high-volume, short-lived, idempotent → Express; long-running, auditable, exactly-once → Standard.","r":["Salah — Exactly-once tidak diperlukan, dan harga per state transition sangat mahal pada 50.000 event per detik.","Benar — Express mendukung laju sangat tinggi, durasi pendek, dan biaya lebih rendah untuk beban seperti ini.","Salah — Standard tetap mahal dan memiliki kuota StartExecution yang jauh di bawah kebutuhan.","Salah — Pola .waitForTaskToken tidak didukung pada Express workflows dan tidak diperlukan."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'high-volume event processing, < 5 menit, at-least-once OK' → Express workflows."},{"id":"E2A-56","d":2,"ts":"2.1.7","t":"Open table formats: Iceberg vs Hive","q":"A data engineering team is comparing Apache Iceberg tables with traditional Hive-style partitioned Parquet tables for a new data lake on Amazon S3. Which TWO capabilities does Apache Iceberg provide that Hive-style tables do not? (Choose TWO.)","o":["ACID transactions with snapshot isolation, so concurrent readers never see partially committed writes","Automatic encryption of all data files with AWS KMS without any bucket or table configuration","Hidden partitioning and partition evolution without rewriting existing data","Guaranteed single-digit millisecond point lookups by primary key","Elimination of the need for any catalog to track table metadata"],"a":[0,2],"e":"Soal ini menguji karakteristik open table format. Apache Iceberg menyimpan metadata, manifest, dan snapshot sehingga setiap commit bersifat atomik dan pembaca melihat snapshot yang konsisten ('ACID transactions with snapshot isolation'). Iceberg juga menyediakan hidden partitioning (partisi dari transformasi kolom, pengguna tidak perlu tahu kolom partisi) dan partition evolution tanpa menulis ulang data. Distraktor terdekat adalah 'eliminates the need for any catalog': Iceberg tetap memerlukan catalog (misalnya AWS Glue Data Catalog atau catalog S3 Tables) untuk menunjuk ke file metadata terkini. Enkripsi KMS adalah fitur S3/bucket, bukan fitur format tabel. Iceberg dioptimalkan untuk scan analitik, bukan point lookup milidetik seperti database key-value. Aturan umum: Iceberg = ACID, time travel, schema & partition evolution, row-level operations di atas file data lake.","r":["Benar — Iceberg memberikan commit atomik dan isolasi snapshot sehingga pembaca tidak pernah melihat tulisan setengah jadi.","Salah — Enkripsi KMS diatur di level S3 atau layanan, bukan fitur bawaan format tabel Iceberg.","Benar — Hidden partitioning dan partition evolution adalah keunggulan utama Iceberg dibanding partisi gaya Hive.","Salah — Iceberg ditujukan untuk analitik skala besar, bukan point lookup milidetik seperti DynamoDB.","Salah — Iceberg tetap memerlukan catalog untuk melacak pointer metadata tabel terkini."],"k":"Iceberg advantages: ACID/snapshot isolation, time travel, schema + partition evolution, row-level ops; still needs a catalog."},{"id":"E1C-62","d":1,"ts":"1.4.7","t":"Lambda EFS configuration requirements","q":"A data engineer is configuring an AWS Lambda function to mount an existing Amazon EFS file system that has mount targets in two private subnets. Which combination of configuration steps is required? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Configure the function to connect to the VPC by using subnets in Availability Zones that have EFS mount targets and a security group that can reach the mount targets on NFS port 2049.","Increase the function's ephemeral storage to 10,240 MB.","Create an EFS access point and add a file system configuration to the function that references the access point and a local mount path under /mnt.","Create an S3 gateway endpoint in the VPC.","Add a user data script to the function that runs the mount command."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Pertanyaannya tentang langkah 'required' untuk me-mount EFS ke Lambda. Fungsi harus terhubung ke VPC dengan subnet di AZ yang memiliki mount target dan security group yang mengizinkan lalu lintas NFS (port 2049) ke mount target, karena EFS hanya diakses melalui jaringan VPC. Lambda me-mount EFS melalui access point, yang ditentukan dalam file system configuration fungsi bersama path lokal yang dimulai dengan /mnt/. Selain itu, execution role memerlukan izin seperti elasticfilesystem:ClientMount (dan ClientWrite untuk menulis). Distractor terdekat adalah S3 gateway endpoint: berguna agar fungsi di VPC bisa mengakses S3, tetapi tidak terkait EFS. Ephemeral storage terpisah dari EFS. Lambda tidak mendukung user data script. Aturan umum: Lambda + EFS = VPC + security group NFS 2049 + access point + mount path /mnt/.","r":["Benar — EFS diakses lewat mount target di VPC, sehingga fungsi harus berada di subnet dan security group yang sesuai.","Salah — /tmp tidak berhubungan dengan mount EFS.","Benar — Lambda me-mount EFS melalui access point dengan path lokal di bawah /mnt.","Salah — Gateway endpoint S3 tidak diperlukan untuk EFS.","Salah — Lambda tidak memiliki user data; mount dilakukan oleh konfigurasi file system."],"k":"Tips ujian: Lambda + EFS → VPC config + access point + mount path /mnt/... (port NFS 2049)."},{"id":"E1C-07","d":1,"ts":"1.3.1","t":"S3 events to Step Functions via EventBridge","q":"A data engineer must start an AWS Step Functions state machine automatically whenever a new object is created under the incoming/ prefix of an Amazon S3 bucket. The solution must not require custom code and must allow filtering on the object key prefix. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Enable Amazon EventBridge notifications on the S3 bucket.","Configure an S3 Event Notification that sends Object Created events directly to the Step Functions state machine.","Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches Object Created events from the bucket with a prefix filter on the object key and sets the state machine as the target.","Create an AWS CloudTrail trail with S3 data events and an Amazon EC2 process that reads the trail logs and starts executions.","Create an Amazon SQS queue for S3 events and an Amazon EC2 instance that polls the queue and calls StartExecution."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Syaratnya 'automatically', 'no custom code', dan 'filtering on the object key prefix'. S3 Event Notifications hanya mendukung tujuan SNS, SQS, Lambda, dan EventBridge — bukan Step Functions secara langsung. Dengan mengaktifkan EventBridge notifications pada bucket, semua event objek dikirim ke EventBridge; lalu aturan EventBridge dengan event pattern (termasuk filter prefix pada object key) dapat menargetkan state machine langsung. Distractor terdekat adalah S3 Event Notification langsung ke Step Functions, yang tidak didukung. Pendekatan CloudTrail data events adalah pola lama yang menambah biaya dan latensi, sedangkan EC2 pemoll antrean adalah kode kustom dan server yang harus dikelola. Aturan umum: S3 → Step Functions tanpa kode = S3 EventBridge notifications + EventBridge rule.","r":["Benar — Mengaktifkan EventBridge notifications membuat event S3 terkirim ke default event bus EventBridge.","Salah — Step Functions bukan destinasi yang didukung S3 Event Notifications (hanya SNS, SQS, Lambda, EventBridge).","Benar — Rule EventBridge dapat memfilter prefix key dan menargetkan state machine tanpa kode.","Salah — CloudTrail data events tidak diperlukan lagi, menambah biaya, dan EC2 adalah kode kustom.","Salah — EC2 yang mem-poll SQS menambah server dan kode yang harus dikelola."],"k":"Tips ujian: S3 event → Step Functions? Aktifkan 'EventBridge notifications' di bucket + rule EventBridge."},{"id":"E3A-58","d":3,"ts":"3.2.3","t":"Redshift materialized views","q":"A Quick Sight dashboard sends the same expensive aggregation query to Amazon Redshift hundreds of times per hour. The query joins a 2-billion-row fact table with three dimension tables and groups the result by day and store. New data is loaded every 30 minutes. The data engineer wants faster dashboard queries with the LEAST maintenance and without changing the dashboard SQL. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Create a regular view with the aggregation query and point the dashboard to it.","Create a materialized view with the aggregation query and AUTO REFRESH YES, and rely on Redshift automatic query rewrite to use it.","Create a new summary table and refresh it with a scheduled TRUNCATE and INSERT every 30 minutes.","Increase the cluster size so that the join completes faster."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'same expensive aggregation query', 'hundreds of times per hour', 'new data every 30 minutes', 'LEAST maintenance', dan 'without changing the dashboard SQL'. Materialized view di Redshift menyimpan hasil query yang sudah dihitung sebelumnya. Dengan AUTO REFRESH YES, Redshift memperbarui view secara otomatis (incremental jika memungkinkan) setelah tabel dasar berubah. Fitur automatic query rewrite membuat query yang memenuhi syarat secara otomatis memakai materialized view, sehingga SQL dashboard tidak perlu diubah. View biasa tetap menjalankan join mahal setiap kali dipanggil. Tabel ringkasan dengan TRUNCATE/INSERT terjadwal membutuhkan pemeliharaan job dan perubahan SQL dashboard. Menambah ukuran cluster mahal dan tetap menghitung ulang query yang sama. Aturan umum: agregasi berulang yang mahal di Redshift → materialized view + auto refresh.","r":["Salah — View biasa tetap menjalankan join dan agregasi penuh setiap kali di-query.","Benar — Materialized view yang di-refresh otomatis dan dipakai lewat automatic query rewrite mempercepat query tanpa mengubah SQL.","Salah — Membutuhkan job terjadwal dan perubahan SQL dashboard ke tabel baru.","Salah — Menambah biaya dan tetap menghitung ulang hasil yang sama ratusan kali."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift 'repeated expensive aggregation' → materialized view + AUTO REFRESH (+ automatic query rewrite)."},{"id":"E2B-58","d":2,"ts":"2.3.6","t":"AWS Backup with Vault Lock","q":"A company runs data stores on Amazon RDS, Amazon DynamoDB, Amazon EFS, and Amazon S3 across 12 AWS accounts. Auditors require a central backup policy with daily backups, 1-year retention, copies stored in a separate backup account, and protection so that nobody, including administrators, can delete the backups before the retention period ends. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Write AWS Lambda functions in each account that create native snapshots and copy them to the backup account.","Use AWS Backup with backup plans managed through AWS Organizations backup policies, cross-account copy to a vault in the backup account, and AWS Backup Vault Lock in compliance mode on that vault.","Enable S3 Cross-Region Replication for every bucket and rely on native automated backups for the databases.","Use AWS Backup in each account with a separate backup plan, and restrict deletion of recovery points with IAM policies."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: berbagai layanan di '12 AWS accounts', 'central backup policy', 'separate backup account', dan 'nobody, including administrators, can delete the backups'. AWS Backup mendukung RDS, DynamoDB, EFS dan S3; dengan backup policy di AWS Organizations, backup plan diterapkan terpusat ke semua akun. Cross-account copy menyimpan salinan di vault milik akun backup. AWS Backup Vault Lock dalam compliance mode membuat recovery point WORM sehingga tidak bisa dihapus siapa pun sebelum retensi berakhir. Backup plan terpisah per akun dengan IAM policy tidak terpusat, dan IAM policy bisa diubah administrator. Lambda kustom adalah overhead besar. CRR dan backup bawaan tidak memberi kebijakan terpusat maupun proteksi WORM. Ingat: backup terpusat multi-layanan, multi-akun, immutable → AWS Backup + Organizations + Vault Lock.","r":["Salah — Lambda kustom di 12 akun adalah overhead besar dan tidak memberi proteksi WORM.","Benar — AWS Backup dengan kebijakan Organizations, cross-account copy dan Vault Lock compliance memenuhi semua syarat.","Salah — Replikasi dan backup bawaan tidak terpusat dan tidak mencegah penghapusan oleh administrator.","Salah — Plan per akun tidak terpusat, dan IAM policy bisa diubah oleh administrator."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'centralized, cross-account, immutable backups' → AWS Backup + Organizations backup policies + Vault Lock."},{"id":"E3B-37","d":3,"ts":"3.3.6","t":"EMR pipeline maintenance - decouple storage and compute","q":"A company runs a long-lived Amazon EMR on EC2 cluster that stores intermediate tables in HDFS. Upgrading to new EMR releases and applying patches is risky because data would be lost if the cluster is replaced, and the cluster is idle for 16 hours each day. Which approach will make the pipeline easier to maintain and MORE cost-effective?","o":["Store the data in Amazon S3 instead of HDFS and run each job on a transient EMR cluster with the latest release that terminates after the job finishes.","Add termination protection and take daily HDFS snapshots to Amazon EBS.","Increase the number of core nodes so that HDFS has more replicas.","Pin the cluster to the current EMR release to avoid upgrades."],"a":[0],"e":"Masalah utamanya adalah 'risky upgrades' karena data di HDFS terikat ke cluster dan 'idle for 16 hours each day'. Dengan menyimpan data di S3 (EMRFS), compute dipisahkan dari storage: setiap job dapat berjalan di cluster transient dengan rilis EMR terbaru, dan cluster dimatikan setelah selesai sehingga tidak membayar waktu idle. Upgrade cukup dengan mengganti versi rilis di definisi cluster. Distraktor terdekat adalah termination protection plus snapshot: tetap membayar cluster idle dan upgrade tetap rumit. Menambah node meningkatkan biaya. Membekukan versi mengabaikan patch keamanan. Aturan: pisahkan storage (S3) dan compute (cluster transient) untuk pipeline EMR yang mudah dirawat.","r":["Benar — Data di S3 membuat cluster bisa dibuang dan dibuat ulang dengan rilis terbaru, serta menghilangkan biaya idle.","Salah — Cluster tetap berjalan saat idle dan upgrade tetap berisiko.","Salah — Menambah node menaikkan biaya tanpa menyelesaikan masalah upgrade.","Salah — Tidak menerapkan patch menimbulkan risiko keamanan dan dukungan."],"k":"Tips ujian: EMR mudah di-upgrade dan murah → data di S3 + transient cluster."},{"id":"E2A-58","d":2,"ts":"2.1.8","t":"OpenSearch k-NN IVF vs HNSW","q":"A company stores 2 billion image embeddings in Amazon OpenSearch Service for a similarity search feature. Keeping an HNSW graph for all vectors in memory would require a very large and expensive cluster. The business can accept slightly lower recall in exchange for much lower memory usage. Which approach should a data engineer use?","o":["Use the Faiss engine with an IVF index combined with product quantization (PQ), and run the training step on a representative sample of vectors before indexing.","Use HNSW with a higher m value to improve recall.","Use exact k-NN with a script score query over all documents.","Store the embeddings as keyword fields and use term queries."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci adalah '2 billion' embedding, HNSW di memori 'very large and expensive', dan bisnis 'can accept slightly lower recall in exchange for much lower memory usage'. Di OpenSearch k-NN, engine Faiss mendukung index IVF yang mengelompokkan vektor ke dalam cluster, dan dapat dikombinasikan dengan product quantization (PQ) untuk mengompresi vektor sehingga jejak memori turun drastis; IVF dan PQ memerlukan model yang dilatih (training API) dengan sampel data representatif sebelum indexing. Distraktor terdekat adalah HNSW dengan m lebih tinggi: recall naik, tetapi memori justru bertambah, berlawanan dengan tujuan. Exact k-NN via script score memindai seluruh dokumen sehingga terlalu lambat untuk 2 miliar vektor. Keyword field tidak mendukung similarity. Aturan umum: skala sangat besar dengan batasan memori → IVF (+PQ) dengan training; recall/latensi terbaik dengan memori cukup → HNSW.","r":["Benar — IVF dengan PQ di Faiss mengurangi memori secara signifikan dengan sedikit penurunan recall, dan memerlukan langkah training.","Salah — Menaikkan m pada HNSW menambah koneksi graph sehingga konsumsi memori justru meningkat.","Salah — Exact k-NN memindai semua vektor sehingga latensinya tidak dapat diterima pada skala miliaran.","Salah — Keyword field dan term query hanya mencocokkan nilai persis, bukan kedekatan vektor."],"k":"Billions of vectors + memory constrained + slight recall loss OK → IVF (+PQ) with training."},{"id":"E4A-47","d":4,"ts":"4.2.4","t":"Lake Formation IAMAllowedPrincipals","q":"A company starts using AWS Lake Formation to manage access to an existing AWS Glue Data Catalog. The data lake administrator grants analysts SELECT on only three tables. However, analysts with broad IAM permissions for glue and athena can still query all tables through Amazon Athena. What should the data lake administrator do so that Lake Formation permissions are enforced?","o":["Delete the analysts' IAM roles and create new roles that have no IAM permissions.","Revoke the Super permission from the IAMAllowedPrincipals group on the existing databases and tables, clear the default settings that use only IAM access control for new databases and tables, and make sure the S3 locations are registered with Lake Formation.","Enable AWS CloudTrail data events for the bucket so that unauthorized queries are blocked.","Encrypt the S3 data with a new KMS key that only the data lake administrator can use."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: Lake Formation baru diaktifkan pada catalog 'existing' dan analis masih bisa membaca semua tabel. Demi kompatibilitas, Lake Formation secara default memberi Super kepada grup virtual IAMAllowedPrincipals pada database dan tabel, sehingga akses tetap ditentukan oleh IAM policy saja. Untuk menegakkan model izin Lake Formation, cabut izin IAMAllowedPrincipals dari resource yang ada, nonaktifkan setting 'Use only IAM access control' untuk database dan tabel baru, dan daftarkan lokasi S3 agar Lake Formation dapat memberikan credential sementara. Menghapus role tidak mengatasi akar masalah. CloudTrail hanya mencatat aktivitas, tidak memblokir. Enkripsi dengan key yang hanya bisa dipakai admin akan memutus akses semua pengguna termasuk yang sah. Aturan umum: grant Lake Formation tidak berefek → cek IAMAllowedPrincipals dan registrasi lokasi data.","r":["Salah — Tidak menyelesaikan akar masalah, yaitu izin IAMAllowedPrincipals yang masih aktif.","Benar — Mencabut IAMAllowedPrincipals dan mengubah default setting membuat izin Lake Formation benar-benar ditegakkan.","Salah — CloudTrail adalah layanan audit dan tidak memblokir query.","Salah — Memutus akses semua pengguna, termasuk analis yang seharusnya bisa membaca tiga tabel."],"k":"Tips ujian: izin Lake Formation 'tidak jalan' → cabut IAMAllowedPrincipals dan matikan 'Use only IAM access control'."},{"id":"E4A-60","d":4,"ts":"4.2.6","t":"Time-bound access with policy conditions","q":"An external consultant needs read access to the s3://analytics-results/q4-review/ prefix through an IAM role that the consultant assumes. Company policy requires that the access automatically stop working after 31 December 2026 without any manual action, and that the consultant cannot read anything else. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Grant the role s3:GetObject on the prefix and create a calendar reminder to delete the role on 31 December 2026.","Set the role's maximum session duration to 12 hours.","Grant the role s3:GetObject on arn:aws:s3:::analytics-results/q4-review/* with a condition that aws:CurrentTime is DateLessThan 2027-01-01T00:00:00Z.","Generate presigned URLs for every object in the prefix with the maximum expiration time."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'automatically stop working after 31 December 2026 without any manual action' dan 'cannot read anything else'. Kondisi aws:CurrentTime dengan operator DateLessThan di custom IAM policy membuat izin hanya berlaku sampai waktu tertentu, sehingga akses otomatis berhenti tanpa tindakan manual. Resource dibatasi ke ARN objek di prefix q4-review/* untuk least privilege. Pengingat kalender bergantung pada tindakan manual. Maximum session duration hanya membatasi lama satu sesi, bukan tanggal akhir akses, karena konsultan dapat meng-assume role lagi. Presigned URL berlaku paling lama 7 hari (dengan credential IAM user dan SigV4; dengan credential role sementara, URL berakhir bersama sesi role) dan tidak mencakup objek baru, sehingga tidak cocok. Aturan umum: akses berbatas waktu → kondisi aws:CurrentTime (DateLessThan/DateGreaterThan).","r":["Salah — Bergantung pada tindakan manual yang bisa terlupa.","Salah — Batas durasi sesi tidak mencegah konsultan meng-assume role lagi setelah tanggal tersebut.","Benar — Kondisi aws:CurrentTime menghentikan akses otomatis dan resource ARN membatasi hanya ke prefix tersebut.","Salah — Presigned URL maksimal 7 hari, tidak mencakup objek baru, dan sulit dikelola."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'access expires on date X automatically' → kondisi aws:CurrentTime DateLessThan di IAM policy."},{"id":"E4B-21","d":4,"ts":"4.3.4","t":"MSK encryption in transit","q":"A company streams payment events through an Amazon MSK provisioned cluster. Security requires that all data be encrypted in transit both between producer or consumer clients and the brokers, and between brokers inside the cluster. Plaintext connections must not be allowed. Which TWO settings should the data engineer configure? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Enable encryption at rest with a customer managed AWS KMS key.","Set client-broker encryption to TLS only.","Set client-broker encryption to TLS_PLAINTEXT so older clients can still connect.","Enable in-cluster (broker-to-broker) encryption.","Restrict the cluster security group to the producers' subnets."],"a":[1,3],"e":"Syaratnya ada dua jalur: 'between producer or consumer clients and the brokers' dan 'between brokers inside the cluster', dengan 'plaintext connections must not be allowed'. Amazon MSK menyediakan pengaturan client-broker encryption (TLS, TLS_PLAINTEXT, atau PLAINTEXT) dan in-cluster encryption terpisah. Memilih TLS only memastikan semua klien wajib memakai TLS, dan mengaktifkan in-cluster encryption mengenkripsi replikasi antar broker. Distraktor terdekat adalah TLS_PLAINTEXT: TLS tersedia, tetapi koneksi plaintext tetap diizinkan sehingga melanggar syarat. Enkripsi at rest dengan KMS penting tetapi tidak berkaitan dengan transit. Security group mengontrol siapa yang terhubung, bukan apakah koneksi terenkripsi. Aturan umum: MSK in transit = client-broker TLS + in-cluster encryption.","r":["Salah — Enkripsi at rest tidak melindungi data yang bergerak antar klien dan broker.","Benar — TLS only menolak koneksi klien plaintext.","Salah — TLS_PLAINTEXT masih mengizinkan koneksi plaintext, melanggar syarat.","Benar — In-cluster encryption mengenkripsi trafik replikasi antar broker.","Salah — Security group membatasi sumber trafik, bukan mengenkripsi koneksi."],"k":"Tips ujian: MSK 'no plaintext' → client-broker = TLS (bukan TLS_PLAINTEXT) + in-cluster encryption on."},{"id":"E2B-47","d":2,"ts":"2.3.4","t":"DynamoDB TTL deletion timing","q":"A DynamoDB table uses TTL to expire temporary access tokens. A security review found that queries sometimes return tokens whose TTL timestamp is already in the past. The application must never treat an expired token as valid. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Add a filter expression to the reads that excludes items whose TTL attribute is earlier than the current time.","Lower the TTL value so that items are deleted sooner.","Switch the table from on-demand to provisioned capacity so that TTL runs faster.","Disable TTL and re-enable it every day to force deletion."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: query 'return tokens whose TTL timestamp is already in the past' dan 'must never treat an expired token as valid'. TTL bersifat asinkron: item yang sudah kedaluwarsa biasanya dihapus dalam beberapa hari, dan sampai benar-benar dihapus item tetap muncul di read, query dan scan. Karena itu aplikasi yang butuh ketepatan harus memfilter item dengan atribut TTL lebih kecil dari waktu sekarang, misalnya lewat filter expression. Menurunkan nilai TTL tidak menjamin waktu penghapusan. Mode kapasitas tidak memengaruhi proses TTL. Mematikan dan menyalakan TTL tidak memaksa penghapusan dan ada jeda saat mengubah setting TTL. Ingat: TTL bukan penghapusan real time → filter item kedaluwarsa di sisi query.","r":["Benar — Filter berdasarkan atribut TTL memastikan item yang sudah kedaluwarsa tetapi belum dihapus tidak dipakai.","Salah — Waktu penghapusan TTL tetap asinkron, jadi item kedaluwarsa masih bisa terbaca.","Salah — Mode kapasitas tidak mengubah kecepatan proses TTL.","Salah — Mengubah status TTL berulang tidak memaksa penghapusan dan bisa mengganggu konfigurasi."],"k":"Tips ujian: TTL menghapus 'eventually' (bisa beberapa hari) → filter atribut TTL di query jika butuh akurasi."},{"id":"E4B-35","d":4,"ts":"4.4.5","t":"Redshift audit logging","q":"An auditor asks a data engineer to provide a record of which database users connected to an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster and which SQL statements they ran over the past 12 months. The records must be queryable with SQL by the audit team without affecting cluster performance. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Enable Amazon Redshift audit logging to Amazon S3, set the enable_user_activity_logging parameter to true in the cluster parameter group, and query the logs with Amazon Athena.","Use AWS CloudTrail management events, because they record every SQL statement that is run on the cluster.","Query the STL_QUERY system table on the cluster whenever the auditor asks for the data.","Enable AWS Config recording for the Redshift cluster."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'which database users connected' dan 'which SQL statements they ran' selama '12 months', dapat di-query SQL 'without affecting cluster performance'. Redshift audit logging menghasilkan connection log, user log, dan user activity log; user activity log (yang mencatat setiap query) hanya aktif bila parameter enable_user_activity_logging = true. Log dikirim ke S3 (atau CloudWatch Logs), sehingga dapat disimpan lama dan di-query dengan Athena tanpa membebani cluster. Ini contoh integrasi beberapa layanan untuk logging audit. Distraktor terdekat adalah STL_QUERY: berisi query, tetapi tabel sistem hanya menyimpan beberapa hari data dan query-nya membebani cluster. CloudTrail hanya mencatat panggilan API Redshift (misalnya CreateCluster), bukan SQL di dalam database. Config merekam konfigurasi cluster, bukan aktivitas pengguna. Aturan umum: audit SQL Redshift jangka panjang → audit logging + enable_user_activity_logging → S3 → Athena.","r":["Benar — Audit logging dengan user activity logging menyimpan koneksi dan SQL ke S3 untuk dianalisis dengan Athena.","Salah — CloudTrail mencatat API manajemen Redshift, bukan pernyataan SQL di database.","Salah — Tabel sistem STL hanya menyimpan beberapa hari data dan query-nya membebani cluster.","Salah — Config melacak perubahan konfigurasi cluster, bukan koneksi atau query pengguna."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'who ran which SQL on Redshift' → audit logging + enable_user_activity_logging; CloudTrail ≠ SQL."},{"id":"E4A-16","d":4,"ts":"4.1.4","t":"CloudFormation service role and iam:PassRole","q":"A data platform team deploys AWS Glue jobs, Glue crawlers, and their IAM roles by using AWS CloudFormation stacks. The security team does not want developers to have permissions to create IAM roles or Glue resources directly, but developers must still be able to create and update the stacks. Which TWO actions should the team take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Attach the AdministratorAccess managed policy to the developers so that stack operations never fail.","Create a CloudFormation service role that has permissions to create the IAM roles and Glue resources, and specify it when creating the stacks.","Pass the CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM capability so that CloudFormation grants developers permissions to create IAM roles.","Apply a stack policy that allows only IAM and Glue resource types to be updated.","Grant the developers cloudformation permissions plus iam:PassRole only for the ARN of the CloudFormation service role."],"a":[1,4],"e":"Kata kunci: developer 'tidak boleh membuat IAM role atau resource Glue langsung' tetapi tetap bisa mengelola stack. CloudFormation service role adalah role yang di-assume CloudFormation untuk membuat resource, sehingga permission besar ada di role tersebut, bukan di developer. Agar developer bisa menunjuk role itu saat membuat stack, mereka butuh iam:PassRole yang dibatasi hanya ke ARN service role tersebut, ditambah permission CloudFormation. CAPABILITY_IAM atau CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM hanyalah pengakuan (acknowledgement) bahwa template membuat resource IAM; ia tidak memberikan permission apa pun. Stack policy hanya melindungi resource dari update yang tidak diinginkan, bukan mengatur siapa yang boleh membuat resource. AdministratorAccess jelas melanggar least privilege. Aturan umum: delegasi deployment = service role + iam:PassRole terbatas.","r":["Salah — AdministratorAccess memberi developer akses penuh, bertentangan dengan kebutuhan keamanan.","Benar — Service role memindahkan permission pembuatan resource ke CloudFormation, bukan ke developer.","Salah — Capability hanya pengakuan bahwa template berisi resource IAM, bukan pemberian permission.","Salah — Stack policy mencegah update tidak sengaja pada resource stack, bukan mekanisme pemberian izin.","Benar — iam:PassRole yang dibatasi ke ARN service role memungkinkan developer memakai role itu tanpa bisa meneruskan role lain."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'users deploy via CloudFormation without direct permissions' → CloudFormation service role + iam:PassRole terbatas."},{"id":"E4B-47","d":4,"ts":"4.5.3","t":"Preventing cross-Region backups","q":"A data engineer discovers that an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster in eu-west-1 has cross-Region snapshot copy enabled to us-east-1, configured years ago for disaster recovery. A new data residency policy requires that backups remain in EU Regions only. Going forward, only the platform team's IAM role may manage snapshot copy settings; the data engineering roles must not be able to re-create the configuration. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Reduce the automated snapshot retention period on the cluster to 1 day.","Disable cross-Region snapshot copy on the cluster, delete the copied snapshots in us-east-1, and attach an IAM policy to the data engineering roles that explicitly denies redshift:EnableSnapshotCopy.","Re-encrypt the cluster with a new AWS KMS key so that the snapshots in us-east-1 cannot be decrypted.","Enable audit logging on the cluster so that snapshot copy operations are recorded."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: backup harus 'remain in EU Regions only' dan hanya role platform yang boleh mengelola snapshot copy ke depannya. Solusi harus korektif sekaligus preventif: menonaktifkan cross-Region snapshot copy menghentikan salinan baru, menghapus snapshot yang sudah ada di us-east-1 menghilangkan data dari Region terlarang, dan IAM policy dengan explicit deny pada redshift:EnableSnapshotCopy untuk role data engineering mencegah konfigurasi itu dibuat ulang (explicit deny selalu mengalahkan allow). Perhatikan bahwa kondisi aws:RequestedRegion tidak cukup di sini: EnableSnapshotCopy dipanggil di Region sumber (eu-west-1) dengan Region tujuan sebagai parameter, sehingga yang perlu ditolak adalah aksinya. Distraktor terdekat adalah re-encrypt dengan KMS key baru: snapshot lama di us-east-1 tetap tersimpan di Region terlarang, sehingga kebijakan residensi tetap dilanggar. Mengurangi retention tidak menghentikan salinan ke us-east-1. Audit logging hanya mencatat, tidak mencegah. Aturan umum: data residency → hentikan replikasi, hapus salinan di Region terlarang, lalu cegah dengan explicit deny pada aksi yang membuat salinan lintas Region (di AWS Organizations kontrol ini bisa juga dipusatkan dengan SCP).","r":["Salah — Retention yang lebih pendek tidak menghentikan salinan snapshot ke us-east-1.","Benar — Menonaktifkan copy, menghapus salinan, dan explicit deny pada redshift:EnableSnapshotCopy memenuhi residensi saat ini dan mencegah konfigurasi dibuat ulang.","Salah — Snapshot tetap tersimpan di Region terlarang meskipun dienkripsi ulang.","Salah — Logging hanya mencatat aktivitas, tidak mencegah atau memperbaiki pelanggaran."],"k":"Tips ujian: data residency violation → disable cross-Region copy/replication + delete copies + explicit deny on the copy/replication action (redshift:EnableSnapshotCopy)."},{"id":"E2C-35","d":2,"ts":"2.4.5","t":"Redshift column compression encodings","q":"A data engineer inherits an Amazon Redshift table of 6 billion rows that was created years ago with all columns set to ENCODE RAW. Disk usage is high and queries scan more data than expected. The engineer wants Redshift to manage column compression with the LEAST ongoing effort. What should the engineer do?","o":["Run ALTER TABLE ... ALTER ENCODE AUTO so that Amazon Redshift chooses and adjusts column encodings automatically.","Export the table to Amazon S3 with UNLOAD and query it with Redshift Spectrum instead.","Change the distribution style of the table to DISTSTYLE ALL.","Run VACUUM FULL every night to reclaim space."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah tabel dengan ENCODE RAW (tanpa kompresi) dan keinginan agar Redshift 'manage column compression with the LEAST ongoing effort'. Compression encoding di Amazon Redshift mengurangi ukuran data di disk dan I/O saat query. Dengan ENCODE AUTO, Redshift memilih encoding yang sesuai (misalnya AZ64 untuk numerik dan tanggal, LZO/ZSTD untuk string) dan dapat menyesuaikannya dari waktu ke waktu, sehingga tidak perlu menjalankan ANALYZE COMPRESSION dan deep copy secara manual. UNLOAD ke S3 dan memakai Spectrum mengubah arsitektur dan tidak mengatasi masalah encoding tabel. DISTSTYLE ALL justru menggandakan data ke setiap node. VACUUM FULL mengurutkan ulang dan mengklaim ruang dari baris terhapus, tetapi tidak mengompres kolom. Aturan umum: kompresi kolom Redshift tanpa effort → ENCODE AUTO (default untuk tabel baru); manual → ANALYZE COMPRESSION.","r":["Benar — ENCODE AUTO membuat Redshift memilih dan menyesuaikan encoding kolom secara otomatis sehingga ukuran dan I/O turun.","Salah — Memindahkan data ke Spectrum mengubah arsitektur dan tidak mengatasi encoding tabel lokal.","Salah — DISTSTYLE ALL menyalin tabel besar ke setiap node dan memperbesar penggunaan disk.","Salah — VACUUM FULL tidak menambahkan kompresi pada kolom RAW."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift kolom tanpa kompresi → ENCODE AUTO (atau ANALYZE COMPRESSION untuk rekomendasi manual)."},{"id":"E3B-31","d":3,"ts":"3.3.4","t":"Redshift WLM and short query acceleration","q":"An Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster uses automatic WLM. Business dashboards run short queries that usually finish in under 5 seconds, but during the nightly ETL window the dashboard queries wait in the queue for minutes behind long-running ETL queries. Short query acceleration (SQA) was turned off when the WLM configuration was customized. The company does not want to add nodes. Which TWO actions will reduce dashboard query wait times? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Enable short query acceleration (SQA).","Assign the ETL user group to a WLM queue with a lower query priority than the dashboard user group's queue.","Run VACUUM FULL on all tables before the ETL window.","Change the distribution style of all tables to ALL.","Resize the cluster to double the number of nodes."],"a":[0,1],"e":"Persyaratannya: query dashboard yang pendek terhambat di antrean di belakang query ETL panjang, dan 'does not want to add nodes'. SQA aktif secara default di parameter group default dan parameter group baru, tetapi di soal ini sempat dimatikan. Short query acceleration (SQA) menjalankan query yang diprediksi pendek di ruang khusus sehingga tidak antre di belakang query panjang. Dengan automatic WLM, menetapkan query priority (misalnya ETL = LOW, dashboard = HIGH) per queue berdasarkan user group membuat Redshift mendahulukan dashboard dalam alokasi sumber daya. Distraktor terdekat adalah resize cluster — memang menambah kapasitas, tetapi melanggar syarat tidak menambah node. VACUUM dan DISTSTYLE ALL tidak menyelesaikan masalah antrean. Aturan: query pendek tertahan → SQA + WLM queues/priority.","r":["Benar — SQA memprioritaskan query pendek sehingga tidak menunggu di belakang query ETL panjang.","Benar — Prioritas query di automatic WLM membuat dashboard mendapat sumber daya lebih dulu daripada ETL.","Salah — VACUUM merapikan baris terhapus dan sort order, bukan masalah antrean query.","Salah — DISTSTYLE ALL memperbesar penyimpanan dan beban load, tidak mengatasi antrean.","Salah — Menambah node melanggar batasan yang diberikan."],"k":"Tips ujian: query dashboard pendek antre di Redshift → SQA + WLM priority/queues."},{"id":"E1C-60","d":1,"ts":"1.4.7","t":"Lambda ephemeral storage","q":"An AWS Lambda function must extract a 3 GB compressed archive, process the extracted files, and then discard them. The data is not needed by any other function or invocation. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead and cost?","o":["Mount an Amazon EFS file system to the function and extract the archive there.","Increase the function's ephemeral storage (/tmp) to a size large enough for the archive and extracted files, up to 10,240 MB.","Attach an Amazon EBS volume to the function.","Split the archive into 512 MB parts and process each part in a separate Lambda function."],"a":[1],"e":"Kebutuhannya: ruang kerja sementara untuk arsip 3 GB, data 'not needed by any other function or invocation', dengan 'LEAST operational overhead and cost'. Lambda menyediakan ephemeral storage /tmp yang dapat dikonfigurasi dari 512 MB hingga 10.240 MB per fungsi; ini cukup untuk arsip dan hasil ekstraksi, tanpa VPC atau layanan tambahan. Distractor terdekat adalah EFS: cocok untuk data yang perlu dibagikan atau persisten, tetapi membutuhkan VPC, mount target, access point, dan biaya penyimpanan, padahal data hanya sementara. EBS tidak dapat dipasang ke Lambda. Memecah arsip menambah orkestrasi dan kompleksitas. Aturan umum: scratch space sementara per invocation → /tmp (hingga 10 GB); data bersama/persisten → EFS.","r":["Salah — EFS menambah VPC, mount target, dan biaya untuk data yang hanya sementara.","Benar — Ephemeral storage hingga 10.240 MB cukup untuk pekerjaan sementara tanpa infrastruktur tambahan.","Salah — Lambda tidak mendukung volume EBS.","Salah — Menambah orkestrasi dan kompleksitas yang tidak perlu."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'temporary large files in Lambda, not shared' → tingkatkan /tmp ephemeral storage (maks 10 GB)."},{"id":"E2C-23","d":2,"ts":"2.4.3","t":"DMS Schema Conversion to Amazon Redshift","q":"A company is moving an on-premises Oracle data warehouse to Amazon Redshift. The data warehouse contains several hundred tables, views, and stored procedures. The data engineer must convert the schema and code to Redshift with the LEAST operational overhead and without managing any conversion servers or desktop software. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Install the AWS Schema Conversion Tool on an Amazon EC2 instance and run the conversion from there.","Use AWS DMS Schema Conversion with an Oracle source data provider and an Amazon Redshift target data provider.","Export the Oracle DDL and run it unchanged against Amazon Redshift.","Use the Amazon Redshift Query Editor v2 to import the Oracle schema directly."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah konversi schema dan kode Oracle ke Amazon Redshift dengan 'LEAST operational overhead' tanpa server atau software desktop. AWS DMS Schema Conversion mendukung jalur Oracle ke Amazon Redshift dan berjalan sebagai fitur terkelola di konsol AWS DMS, memakai instance profile, data provider, dan migration project. AWS SCT memang dapat melakukan konversi yang sama, tetapi harus diinstal dan dikelola di mesin sendiri atau EC2, yang menambah overhead; AWS SCT juga dihapus dari daftar in-scope services pada exam guide versi 1.1 (meski masih disebut sebagai contoh di skill 2.4.3). DDL Oracle tidak kompatibel langsung dengan Redshift (tipe data, sintaks prosedur, distribution/sort key). Query Editor v2 adalah alat untuk menjalankan query, bukan konversi schema heterogen. Aturan umum: konversi schema heterogen dengan sedikit overhead → DMS Schema Conversion (pengganti terkelola untuk AWS SCT).","r":["Salah — SCT di EC2 berhasil, tetapi menambah server dan software yang harus dikelola sendiri.","Benar — DMS Schema Conversion mendukung Oracle ke Redshift sebagai layanan terkelola tanpa server sendiri.","Salah — DDL dan prosedur Oracle tidak kompatibel langsung dengan Redshift.","Salah — Query Editor v2 tidak melakukan konversi schema dan kode dari Oracle."],"k":"Tips ujian: konversi schema heterogen tanpa instal tool → AWS DMS Schema Conversion (bukan SCT di EC2)."},{"id":"E3B-12","d":3,"ts":"3.3.5","t":"CloudTrail data events","q":"A company has an existing CloudTrail trail. The security team discovers that no S3 GetObject calls on the 'pii-curated' bucket appear in the logs, although analysts read objects from it daily. The company wants to capture these reads while keeping CloudTrail costs as low as possible. The account contains 300 other buckets. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Enable CloudTrail Insights on the trail.","Enable data events for all current and future S3 buckets on the trail.","Add an advanced event selector for S3 data events that is limited to the 'pii-curated' bucket ARN and read-only events.","Enable log file integrity validation on the trail."],"a":[2],"e":"Penyebab masalahnya: secara default trail hanya merekam management events; operasi objek S3 seperti GetObject adalah data events yang harus diaktifkan terpisah dan dikenai biaya per event. Persyaratan 'as low as possible' dengan '300 other buckets' berarti harus difilter. Advanced event selector dapat membatasi data events hanya untuk ARN bucket 'pii-curated' dan hanya event read-only, sehingga biaya minimal. Distraktor terdekat adalah mengaktifkan data events untuk semua bucket — berfungsi, tetapi biayanya jauh lebih tinggi. Insights dan integrity validation tidak menambah perekaman data events. Aturan: object-level S3 activity → data events, gunakan selector untuk mengontrol biaya.","r":["Salah — Insights mendeteksi anomali management events, tidak merekam GetObject.","Salah — Merekam data events semua bucket akan menambah biaya besar yang tidak perlu.","Benar — Advanced event selector membatasi data events ke satu bucket dan operasi baca, sehingga biaya tetap rendah.","Salah — Integrity validation membuktikan keaslian file log, tidak menambah jenis event yang direkam."],"k":"Tips ujian: GetObject/PutObject tidak muncul di CloudTrail → aktifkan data events (filter dengan advanced event selectors)."},{"id":"E1C-48","d":1,"ts":"1.4.1","t":"Glue push-down predicates","q":"An AWS Glue ETL script reads a Data Catalog table that is partitioned by year, month, and day and contains 5 years of data. The script loads the entire table into a DynamicFrame and then filters it to keep only yesterday's partition. The job takes 2 hours. Which change will reduce the runtime the MOST?","o":["Add more workers to the job.","Use the push_down_predicate option when creating the DynamicFrame from the catalog so that only yesterday's partition is read.","Convert the DynamicFrame to a DataFrame before applying the filter.","Run an AWS Glue crawler before the job to refresh partitions."],"a":[1],"e":"Masalah utamanya: script 'loads the entire table' lima tahun lalu memfilter satu hari. Opsi push_down_predicate pada create_dynamic_frame.from_catalog menerapkan filter pada kolom partisi sebelum data dibaca, sehingga Glue hanya membaca file dari partisi yang cocok (partition pruning) dan sisanya tidak pernah dipindai. Distractor terdekat adalah menambah worker: membaca lima tahun data menjadi lebih cepat, tetapi tetap membaca data yang tidak perlu dan biaya naik. Konversi ke DataFrame sebelum filter tetap membaca seluruh data. Crawler hanya memperbarui metadata partisi. Aturan umum: filter data terpartisi sedini mungkin di sumber — push_down_predicate di Glue, WHERE pada kolom partisi di Athena.","r":["Salah — Lebih banyak worker tetap membaca seluruh data lima tahun dan menambah biaya.","Benar — Push-down predicate hanya membaca partisi kemarin sehingga I/O turun drastis.","Salah — Filter setelah pembacaan tetap memindai seluruh tabel.","Salah — Crawler memperbarui metadata, bukan mengurangi data yang dibaca."],"k":"Tips ujian: Glue membaca tabel terpartisi lalu filter → push_down_predicate."},{"id":"E1A-22","d":1,"ts":"1.1.3","t":"Data Firehose buffering hints","q":"An Amazon Data Firehose stream delivers JSON events to Amazon S3 for querying with Amazon Athena. The stream uses default buffering, and the data lake now contains a very large number of small objects, which makes Athena queries slow. Data freshness of up to 15 minutes is acceptable. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Increase the Firehose buffer size and buffer interval (up to 128 MB and 900 seconds) so that fewer, larger objects are written.","Lower the buffer interval to 60 seconds so that files are written more often.","Replace Firehose with an AWS Lambda function that writes each event as a separate object.","Enable S3 Versioning on the destination bucket."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'very large number of small objects' memperlambat Athena dan 'data freshness of up to 15 minutes is acceptable'. Firehose mengirim objek ke S3 setiap kali salah satu buffering hint (ukuran atau interval) terpenuhi lebih dulu. Menaikkan buffer size dan buffer interval (untuk tujuan S3: buffer size 1–128 MB dan interval 0–900 detik, default 5 MB dan 300 detik; interval 0 = zero buffering untuk latensi rendah) menghasilkan objek yang lebih sedikit dan lebih besar, sehingga Athena membuka lebih sedikit file. Toleransi 15 menit memungkinkan interval 900 detik. Distraktor terdekat adalah menurunkan interval: justru memperbanyak file kecil. Lambda per event memperparah small files, dan versioning tidak mengubah ukuran objek. Aturan umum: trade-off Firehose = buffer lebih besar → file lebih besar dan lebih sedikit, tetapi latensi lebih tinggi.","r":["Benar — Buffer lebih besar dan lebih lama menghasilkan objek lebih besar dan lebih sedikit, masih dalam toleransi 15 menit.","Salah — Interval lebih pendek menghasilkan lebih banyak file kecil.","Salah — Satu objek per event memperparah masalah file kecil.","Salah — Versioning tidak memengaruhi ukuran atau jumlah objek yang ditulis Firehose."],"k":"Firehose → banyak file kecil → naikkan buffer size/interval (trade-off dengan latensi)."},{"id":"E3A-46","d":3,"ts":"3.2.4","t":"Exploring catalog data in Athena Spark notebooks","q":"In an Amazon Athena notebook with the Apache Spark engine, a data engineer wants to explore a 2 TB clickstream table that is registered in the AWS Glue Data Catalog and plot daily active users for the last 90 days as a line chart inside the notebook. Which approach is MOST appropriate?","o":["Copy the 2 TB of files to the notebook's local disk and read them with pandas.","Call toPandas() on the full 2 TB table and then aggregate and plot the data with matplotlib.","Export the table to CSV with Athena SQL and open the file in a spreadsheet application.","Use spark.sql() to query the Glue Data Catalog table and aggregate daily active users in Spark, convert the small 90-row result to pandas, and plot it with matplotlib in the notebook."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kuncinya '2 TB table', 'registered in the Glue Data Catalog', dan 'plot 90 days inside the notebook'. Athena Spark terintegrasi dengan Glue Data Catalog, sehingga tabel bisa langsung di-query dengan spark.sql(). Prinsip pentingnya: lakukan agregasi berat secara terdistribusi di Spark, lalu bawa hanya hasil kecil (90 baris) ke driver dengan toPandas() untuk divisualisasikan dengan matplotlib di notebook. Memanggil toPandas() pada 2 TB memindahkan semua data ke driver dan pasti gagal karena kehabisan memori. Menyalin 2 TB ke disk lokal tidak mungkin dan membuang manfaat Spark. Ekspor ke CSV dan spreadsheet tidak mampu menampung volume ini dan keluar dari notebook. Aturan umum: agregasi di Spark, visualisasi hanya atas hasil yang kecil.","r":["Salah — Notebook tidak dirancang untuk menyalin 2 TB ke disk lokal, dan pandas tidak terdistribusi.","Salah — toPandas() pada 2 TB memindahkan seluruh data ke driver dan menyebabkan out-of-memory.","Salah — Spreadsheet tidak mampu menampung data sebesar ini dan langkahnya manual.","Benar — Agregasi terdistribusi di Spark lalu plot hasil kecil dengan matplotlib adalah pola yang benar."],"k":"Tips ujian: notebook Spark + visualisasi → agregasi di Spark dulu, baru toPandas() pada hasil kecil."},{"id":"E2A-12","d":2,"ts":"2.1.2","t":"Redshift sort keys","q":"An Amazon Redshift table stores 3 years of IoT events. Nearly all queries filter on a range of event_date, usually the most recent 7 days, and sometimes also filter on device_type. New data is loaded daily in event_date order. Which table design improves query performance the MOST?","o":["Define an interleaved sort key on six columns, including event_date and device_type.","Use DISTSTYLE KEY on event_date and no sort key.","Define a compound sort key with event_date as the leading column, followed by device_type.","Use DISTSTYLE ALL so every node has a full copy of the table."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'nearly all queries filter on a range of event_date' dan data dimuat 'in event_date order'. Compound sort key dengan event_date sebagai kolom pertama membuat zone map pada setiap blok sangat efektif, sehingga Redshift melewati (skip) blok yang di luar rentang tanggal; device_type sebagai kolom kedua membantu filter tambahan. Karena data dimuat berurutan, tabel tetap tersortir tanpa VACUUM berat. Distraktor terdekat adalah interleaved sort key: memberi bobot sama ke banyak kolom, berguna jika filter bervariasi, tetapi lebih lambat untuk load dan butuh VACUUM REINDEX, serta kurang efektif untuk data yang terus bertambah berdasarkan tanggal. DISTKEY pada tanggal menyebabkan skew (data hari ini di satu slice) dan tidak menggantikan sort key. Aturan umum: filter rentang dominan pada satu kolom → compound sort key dengan kolom itu di depan.","r":["Salah — Interleaved sort key untuk banyak kolom mahal dipelihara (VACUUM REINDEX) dan tidak optimal ketika satu kolom filter mendominasi.","Salah — Distribusi berdasarkan tanggal menimbulkan skew dan tanpa sort key Redshift tidak bisa melewati blok berdasarkan rentang tanggal.","Benar — Compound sort key dengan event_date di depan memaksimalkan block skipping via zone map untuk filter rentang tanggal.","Salah — DISTSTYLE ALL tidak membantu filter, dan menyalin tabel besar ke semua node sangat boros."],"k":"Range filter dominan pada satu kolom (tanggal) → compound sort key, kolom itu di posisi pertama."},{"id":"E1A-33","d":1,"ts":"1.1.5","t":"AWS Glue workflows and triggers","q":"A nightly pipeline must run an AWS Glue crawler on raw data, then run an AWS Glue ETL job only if the crawler succeeds, and finally run a second crawler on the curated output after the job succeeds. The data engineer wants to use only AWS Glue features. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create three independent scheduled triggers that start the crawler at 00:00, the job at 00:30, and the second crawler at 01:30.","Create an AWS Glue workflow with a scheduled trigger that starts the first crawler, and conditional triggers that start the job and the second crawler when the previous step succeeds.","Use Amazon S3 Event Notifications to start each component when objects are written.","Configure the ETL job to call the crawlers from inside the job script."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: urutan 'crawler → job → crawler', 'only if ... succeeds', dan 'use only AWS Glue features'. AWS Glue workflow mengorkestrasi crawler dan job dalam satu graf: scheduled trigger memulai workflow, lalu conditional trigger menjalankan langkah berikutnya saat langkah sebelumnya mencapai status SUCCEEDED. Distraktor terdekat adalah tiga trigger terjadwal dengan jeda waktu: tidak ada jaminan langkah sebelumnya selesai atau sukses, sehingga rentan race condition. S3 Event Notifications tidak tahu status sukses crawler. Memanggil crawler dari dalam script mencampur orkestrasi dengan logika ETL. Aturan umum: dependensi antar job/crawler Glue = Glue workflow dengan conditional triggers.","r":["Salah — Jeda waktu tetap tidak menjamin langkah sebelumnya sudah selesai dan sukses.","Benar — Glue workflow dengan conditional trigger menjalankan langkah berikutnya hanya setelah langkah sebelumnya sukses.","Salah — S3 events tidak mencerminkan status sukses crawler atau job.","Salah — Mencampur orkestrasi ke dalam script ETL menyulitkan pemantauan dan penanganan error."],"k":"Rantai crawler/job Glue dengan kondisi sukses → Glue workflow + conditional triggers."},{"id":"E3A-24","d":3,"ts":"3.1.6","t":"SageMaker Unified Studio data preparation","q":"A company has data engineers who build ETL flows and data analysts who explore data with SQL and Python notebooks. Today each group uses separate consoles (AWS Glue Studio, Amazon Athena, and Amazon EMR Studio) with separately managed permissions. The company wants one governed workspace where both groups collaborate in shared projects, prepare data with visual ETL flows, and query the results with SQL or notebooks. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Deploy JupyterHub on an Amazon EKS cluster and give both groups access to shared notebooks.","Create separate AWS accounts for each team and share data with S3 bucket policies.","Set up Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio with a domain and shared projects, and use its visual ETL, query editor, and notebook capabilities.","Give both teams access to an Amazon EMR on EC2 cluster with Apache Zeppelin installed."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'one governed workspace', 'shared projects', 'visual ETL flows', serta query dengan 'SQL or notebooks'. Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio menyatukan alat data dan AI dalam satu lingkungan: domain dan project sebagai unit kolaborasi dan izin, visual ETL (berbasis AWS Glue) untuk persiapan data, query editor (Athena/Redshift), serta notebook JupyterLab. Akses data diatur melalui project dan SageMaker Catalog, sehingga izin tidak lagi dikelola terpisah per konsol. JupyterHub di EKS adalah solusi self-managed dengan overhead tinggi dan tanpa visual ETL. Akun terpisah dengan bucket policy justru memecah kolaborasi. EMR dengan Zeppelin menambah pengelolaan cluster dan tidak menyediakan visual ETL maupun tata kelola project. Aturan umum: 'unified workspace + projects + visual ETL + SQL + notebook' → SageMaker Unified Studio.","r":["Salah — JupyterHub di EKS harus dikelola sendiri dan tidak menyediakan visual ETL atau tata kelola project.","Salah — Akun terpisah memecah kolaborasi dan menambah kerumitan izin.","Benar — Unified Studio menyediakan project bersama, visual ETL, query editor, dan notebook dalam satu lingkungan terkelola.","Salah — Cluster EMR dengan Zeppelin menambah overhead dan tidak punya visual ETL atau project governance."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'single workspace untuk engineer + analis, project, visual ETL, SQL, notebook' → Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio."},{"id":"E3A-20","d":3,"ts":"3.1.5","t":"Consuming third-party data APIs","q":"An AWS Lambda function runs every 15 minutes to pull exchange-rate data from a third-party REST API and store it in Amazon S3. The API requires an API key, returns results in pages with a next-page token, and returns HTTP 429 when the client exceeds its rate limit. Recently, some runs stored incomplete data. Which TWO changes should the data engineer make? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Store the API key in AWS Secrets Manager and retrieve it at runtime instead of hardcoding it.","Follow the next-page token until no token is returned before writing the dataset as complete.","Increase the Lambda function memory to 10 GB so that each request returns more records.","Handle HTTP 429 responses by retrying with exponential backoff and jitter, honoring any Retry-After header.","Call the API from 50 concurrent Lambda invocations to finish faster."],"a":[1,3],"e":"Masalahnya 'incomplete data' dengan dua penyebab yang tersirat di stem: API memakai pagination dengan 'next-page token' dan mengembalikan 'HTTP 429' saat melewati rate limit. Untuk memastikan data lengkap, kode harus terus mengikuti next-page token sampai tidak ada token lagi. Respons 429 harus ditangani dengan retry memakai exponential backoff dan jitter (serta header Retry-After jika ada), bukan diabaikan. Menyimpan API key di Secrets Manager adalah praktik keamanan yang baik, tetapi tidak menyelesaikan masalah data yang tidak lengkap. Memori Lambda tidak mengubah ukuran halaman yang dikembalikan API pihak ketiga. Menjalankan 50 invocation paralel justru memicu lebih banyak 429. Aturan umum saat mengonsumsi API data: tangani pagination, rate limit (429) dengan backoff, dan idempotensi.","r":["Salah — Praktik keamanan yang baik, tetapi tidak memperbaiki data yang tidak lengkap.","Benar — Mengikuti next-page token sampai habis memastikan semua halaman terambil.","Salah — Memori Lambda tidak mengubah jumlah record per halaman dari API pihak ketiga.","Benar — Retry dengan backoff untuk HTTP 429 mencegah halaman yang terlewat karena rate limit.","Salah — Concurrency tinggi memperparah rate limiting dan menambah respons 429."],"k":"Tips ujian: konsumsi API pihak ketiga → ikuti pagination token + backoff untuk HTTP 429."},{"id":"E2A-46","d":2,"ts":"2.1.6","t":"Redshift lock troubleshooting","q":"A nightly ETL job in Amazon Redshift has been waiting for over an hour on an ALTER TABLE statement. A data engineer suspects that another session is holding a lock on the table. What should the data engineer do to find and resolve the blocking session?","o":["Query STV_LOCKS and SVV_TRANSACTIONS to identify the session holding the lock, and then call PG_TERMINATE_BACKEND with that process ID.","Reboot the Redshift cluster to release all locks.","Run VACUUM FULL on the table to remove the lock.","Run ANALYZE on the table so the query planner can bypass the lock."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci adalah ALTER TABLE yang 'waiting' dan dugaan 'another session is holding a lock'. ALTER TABLE memerlukan AccessExclusiveLock, sehingga ia menunggu jika sesi lain (misalnya transaksi yang belum di-commit atau query panjang) memegang lock pada tabel tersebut. Tabel sistem STV_LOCKS dan view SVV_TRANSACTIONS menunjukkan lock yang dipegang dan ditunggu beserta PID-nya, lalu PG_TERMINATE_BACKEND(pid) menghentikan sesi penghalang sehingga transaksinya di-rollback dan lock dilepas. Distraktor terdekat adalah reboot cluster: memang melepas semua lock, tetapi mengganggu semua pengguna dan workload lain secara berlebihan. VACUUM dan ANALYZE adalah operasi pemeliharaan yang tidak melepas lock dan justru dapat ikut menunggu. Aturan umum: lock contention di Redshift → identifikasi via STV_LOCKS/SVV_TRANSACTIONS, selesaikan via PG_TERMINATE_BACKEND.","r":["Benar — STV_LOCKS dan SVV_TRANSACTIONS menunjukkan pemegang lock, dan PG_TERMINATE_BACKEND menghentikan sesi tersebut secara tertarget.","Salah — Reboot menghentikan seluruh workload cluster; tindakan berlebihan untuk satu sesi penghalang.","Salah — VACUUM tidak melepas lock milik sesi lain dan bisa ikut menunggu lock.","Salah — ANALYZE hanya memperbarui statistik; tidak ada cara bagi planner untuk melewati lock."],"k":"Redshift blocked by lock → STV_LOCKS / SVV_TRANSACTIONS to find PID → PG_TERMINATE_BACKEND(pid)."},{"id":"E1B-57","d":1,"ts":"1.2.8","t":"API Gateway caching for data APIs","q":"A company exposes daily sales aggregates through an Amazon API Gateway REST API. Each request invokes an AWS Lambda function that runs an Amazon Athena query. The aggregates change only once per day, but the API receives thousands of identical requests per hour, causing high Athena costs and slow responses. Which solution will MOST reduce cost and latency with the LEAST effort?","o":["Enable provisioned concurrency for the Lambda function.","Increase the memory of the Lambda function to 10 GB.","Add Amazon DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) in front of Athena.","Enable API Gateway caching on the stage with the maximum time-to-live of 1 hour (3,600 seconds)."],"a":[3],"e":"Penentunya adalah data yang 'change only once per day' tetapi menerima 'thousands of identical requests per hour', sehingga Athena dijalankan berulang untuk hasil yang sama. API Gateway stage caching menyimpan respons di tingkat API untuk TTL tertentu (default 300 detik, maksimum 3.600 detik), sehingga request identik dilayani dari cache tanpa memanggil Lambda dan Athena; dengan TTL 1 jam, ribuan request identik per jam hanya memicu sekitar satu query Athena per jam per cache key, jadi biaya dan latensi turun drastis dengan konfigurasi sederhana. Provisioned concurrency hanya menghilangkan cold start Lambda, tetapi setiap request tetap menjalankan query Athena. Menaikkan memori Lambda tidak mempercepat Athena dan menaikkan biaya. DAX adalah cache khusus DynamoDB dan tidak bisa dipasang di depan Athena. Aturan umum: respons API yang sama berulang dan jarang berubah → API Gateway caching.","r":["Salah — Mengurangi cold start, tetapi query Athena tetap berjalan untuk setiap request.","Salah — Memori Lambda tidak mempercepat query Athena dan menambah biaya.","Salah — DAX hanya untuk DynamoDB, tidak untuk Athena.","Benar — Caching di API Gateway (TTL maksimum 1 jam) melayani request identik tanpa memanggil backend selama TTL."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'many identical API requests, data changes rarely' → API Gateway caching (TTL default 300 s, maksimum 3.600 s)."},{"id":"E2B-23","d":2,"ts":"2.2.5","t":"Glue connections to on-premises sources","q":"A company has an on-premises Oracle database that is reachable from its AWS VPC through AWS Direct Connect. The data engineering team wants to catalog the Oracle tables in the AWS Glue Data Catalog and run AWS Glue ETL jobs that read directly from the database. Copying the database to AWS first is not allowed. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create an AWS Glue JDBC connection for the Oracle database in a VPC subnet that routes to the on-premises network, allow the database port in the security group and the on-premises firewall, and use the connection in a crawler and the ETL jobs.","Use AWS DMS to perform a full load of the database into Amazon S3, and crawl the S3 data.","Create an AWS Glue connection of type NETWORK in a public subnet and connect to the database's public IP address over the internet.","Use Amazon Athena Federated Query to read the Oracle tables and run CTAS queries to create Data Catalog tables."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'reachable ... through AWS Direct Connect', 'catalog the Oracle tables' dan 'Copying the database to AWS first is not allowed'. Glue JDBC connection bisa terhubung ke database on-premises selama subnet yang dipilih punya rute ke jaringan on-premises (Direct Connect atau VPN) dan port database diizinkan di security group serta firewall on-premises. Connection yang sama dipakai crawler untuk mengisi Data Catalog dan oleh ETL job untuk membaca langsung. DMS full load menyalin data ke S3, yang dilarang. Koneksi lewat internet ke IP publik melanggar praktik keamanan dan mengabaikan Direct Connect yang sudah ada. Athena CTAS juga menyalin data. Ingat: sumber on-premises untuk Glue → JDBC connection di subnet VPC yang terhubung lewat DX/VPN.","r":["Benar — JDBC connection melalui Direct Connect memungkinkan crawler dan job membaca Oracle langsung tanpa menyalin data.","Salah — DMS full load menyalin database ke S3, yang dilarang skenario.","Salah — Mengekspos database ke internet tidak aman, dan tipe NETWORK tidak membawa detail JDBC untuk crawler.","Salah — CTAS menulis salinan data ke S3, dan Federated Query tidak membuat definisi tabel sumber di Data Catalog."],"k":"Tips ujian: Glue ke database on-premises → JDBC connection di subnet VPC dengan rute DX/VPN + SG/firewall."},{"id":"E2C-50","d":2,"ts":"2.4.5","t":"Data skipping with sorted Parquet files","q":"An Amazon Athena table stores sensor data as Parquet files partitioned by date. Most queries filter on device_id within a single day, but each daily partition contains 2,000 files and device_id values are spread randomly across all files, so Athena reads almost every file. The data engineer wants to reduce the data scanned without adding more partition columns. Which technique should the engineer apply when writing the data?","o":["Write the data sorted (clustered) by device_id within each partition so that Parquet min/max statistics allow Athena to skip row groups and files.","Convert the files from Parquet to CSV so that Athena can split them more easily.","Add a partition column for device_id with 500,000 distinct values.","Disable compression so that Athena can read the files faster."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah filter device_id dalam satu partisi, nilai device_id tersebar acak di semua file, dan syarat 'without adding more partition columns'. File Parquet menyimpan statistik min/max per row group, yang dipakai Athena untuk predicate pushdown; jika data diurutkan (atau di-cluster/bucket) berdasarkan device_id saat penulisan, setiap file dan row group hanya mencakup range device_id yang sempit sehingga sebagian besar dapat dilewati. Konversi ke CSV menghilangkan statistik kolumnar dan menambah data yang dipindai. Partisi device_id dengan 500.000 nilai melanggar syarat dan menimbulkan ledakan partisi. Menonaktifkan kompresi memperbesar data yang dipindai sehingga biaya naik. Aturan umum: data skipping di Parquet/ORC bergantung pada sort/clustering kolom filter, bukan hanya partisi.","r":["Benar — Data yang terurut berdasarkan device_id membuat statistik min/max efektif untuk melewati row group dan file.","Salah — CSV tidak memiliki statistik kolom sehingga semua data harus dibaca.","Salah — Partisi berkardinalitas sangat tinggi melanggar syarat dan menimbulkan masalah small files.","Salah — Tanpa kompresi, volume data yang dipindai justru bertambah."],"k":"Tips ujian: kurangi scan tanpa partisi baru → sort/cluster data pada kolom filter agar min/max stats Parquet efektif."},{"id":"E1A-57","d":1,"ts":"1.1.9","t":"Rate limiting third-party APIs with SQS and Lambda","q":"An Amazon SQS queue receives customer IDs that must be enriched by calling a third-party API. The API enforces a strict limit of about 20 concurrent requests and returns HTTP 429 errors when the limit is exceeded. A Lambda function consumes the queue, and during backlogs it scales out and exceeds the API limit. What is the BEST way to respect the rate limit while keeping the backlog safe?","o":["Increase the SQS visibility timeout to 12 hours.","Configure the maximum concurrency setting on the SQS event source mapping to limit concurrent invocations, and use retries with backoff for 429 responses.","Switch the queue to a FIFO queue and use a single message group for all messages.","Delete messages that receive a 429 response so that the queue drains faster."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: API membatasi 'about 20 concurrent requests', error '429', Lambda 'scales out' saat backlog, dan 'keeping the backlog safe'. Setting maximum concurrency pada event source mapping SQS membatasi jumlah invocation Lambda bersamaan yang dipicu oleh antrean tersebut, sehingga beban ke API tetap di bawah batas; pesan yang belum diproses tetap aman di antrean. Retry dengan backoff untuk respons 429 menangani lonjakan sesaat. Distraktor terdekat adalah FIFO dengan satu message group: hanya satu pesan diproses pada satu waktu sehingga throughput jauh di bawah batas yang diizinkan. Visibility timeout yang sangat panjang menunda retry pesan yang gagal. Menghapus pesan yang terkena 429 menyebabkan kehilangan data. Aturan umum: melindungi downstream yang rate-limited = buffer dengan SQS + batasi concurrency consumer + backoff.","r":["Salah — Visibility timeout panjang hanya menunda retry dan tidak membatasi concurrency.","Benar — Maximum concurrency membatasi invocation bersamaan sesuai batas API, dan backlog tetap aman di antrean.","Salah — Satu message group memproses satu pesan pada satu waktu sehingga throughput terlalu rendah.","Salah — Menghapus pesan yang gagal menyebabkan kehilangan data."],"k":"Downstream API rate-limited → SQS buffer + maximum concurrency pada ESM + backoff untuk 429."},{"id":"E3A-35","d":3,"ts":"3.1.9","t":"EventBridge Glue state change events","q":"A company runs dozens of AWS Glue jobs. The on-call team must receive an email whenever any Glue job run ends in the FAILED or TIMEOUT state. The solution must not require changes to the job scripts. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST effort?","o":["Add try/except blocks to every Glue script that publish a message to Amazon SNS when an exception occurs.","Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches Glue Job State Change events with state FAILED or TIMEOUT and targets an Amazon SNS topic with an email subscription.","Run an AWS Lambda function every 5 minutes that calls GetJobRuns for every job and sends an email for failed runs.","Create an AWS CloudTrail trail and search the logs daily for StartJobRun errors."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'any Glue job', 'FAILED or TIMEOUT', dan 'no changes to the job scripts'. AWS Glue otomatis mengirim event 'Glue Job State Change' ke default event bus EventBridge. Rule dengan event pattern pada field state (FAILED, TIMEOUT) bisa langsung menargetkan topic SNS yang memiliki subscription email. Tanpa kode, tanpa perubahan script, dan berlaku untuk semua job. Try/except di setiap script mengubah kode dan tidak menangkap timeout. Lambda polling menambah kode dan jeda waktu. CloudTrail mencatat panggilan API seperti StartJobRun, bukan hasil akhir run, dan pencarian harian terlalu lambat. Aturan umum: bereaksi pada perubahan status layanan AWS (Glue, EMR, Step Functions) → rule EventBridge pada event state change.","r":["Salah — Mengubah setiap script dan tidak menangkap status TIMEOUT.","Benar — Rule EventBridge pada Glue Job State Change ke SNS bekerja untuk semua job tanpa kode.","Salah — Polling menambah kode, biaya, dan keterlambatan notifikasi.","Salah — CloudTrail mencatat panggilan API, bukan status akhir job run, dan pencarian harian terlambat."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'notify when Glue job fails, no code change' → EventBridge rule (Glue Job State Change) → SNS."},{"id":"E2B-35","d":2,"ts":"2.3.2","t":"S3 Lifecycle transitions between storage classes","q":"A company stores application logs in Amazon S3 Standard. Logs are read frequently for 30 days and are rarely read from day 31 through day 365, but when they are needed during that period they must be returned in milliseconds. After 1 year, logs must be kept for 6 more years for compliance, and retrieval within 48 hours is acceptable. Which S3 Lifecycle configuration is the MOST cost-effective?","o":["Transition to S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval after 30 days and to S3 Glacier Deep Archive after 365 days.","Transition to S3 One Zone-IA after 30 days and to S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval after 365 days.","Transition to S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval after 30 days and to S3 Glacier Deep Archive after 365 days.","Keep the objects in S3 Standard for 365 days and then transition them to S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'rarely read' tetapi harus kembali 'in milliseconds' pada hari 31–365, lalu disimpan 6 tahun dengan pengambilan 'within 48 hours'. S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval memberi akses milidetik dengan biaya penyimpanan lebih rendah daripada Standard-IA untuk data yang diakses sekitar sekali per kuartal atau lebih jarang. Untuk arsip jangka panjang dengan pengambilan dalam 48 jam, S3 Glacier Deep Archive adalah kelas termurah (standard retrieval sekitar 12 jam, bulk sekitar 48 jam). Glacier Flexible Retrieval di hari ke-30 melanggar syarat milidetik. One Zone-IA hanya satu AZ dan Glacier Flexible Retrieval lebih mahal daripada Deep Archive untuk arsip 6 tahun. Menyimpan di Standard selama 365 hari terlalu mahal. Ingat: rarely + milliseconds → Glacier Instant Retrieval; archive + 12–48 jam → Deep Archive.","r":["Benar — Glacier Instant Retrieval memenuhi akses milidetik dengan biaya rendah, dan Deep Archive adalah arsip termurah untuk 6 tahun.","Salah — One Zone-IA kurang tahan terhadap kehilangan AZ, dan Glacier Flexible Retrieval lebih mahal daripada Deep Archive untuk arsip.","Salah — Glacier Flexible Retrieval butuh menit hingga jam, sehingga melanggar syarat milidetik.","Salah — Standard selama setahun untuk data yang jarang dibaca jauh lebih mahal."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'rarely accessed' + 'milliseconds' → Glacier Instant Retrieval; 'archive' + 'hours ok' → Glacier Deep Archive."},{"id":"E4A-36","d":4,"ts":"4.2.2","t":"Glue connection with Secrets Manager","q":"A data engineer creates an AWS Glue JDBC connection to an on-premises Microsoft SQL Server database. The username and password are currently typed directly into the connection properties, and several engineers can view them in the console. The company wants to stop exposing the credentials while keeping the Glue jobs working with minimal changes. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Pass the username and password as job parameters when each Glue job starts.","Store the credentials in a Systems Manager Parameter Store String parameter and read it at the start of each job script.","Store the credentials in AWS Secrets Manager, configure the Glue connection to use the secret, and allow the Glue job role secretsmanager:GetSecretValue on that secret.","Save the credentials in a text file in an Amazon S3 bucket that only the Glue job role can read."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'stop exposing the credentials' dan 'minimal changes'. AWS Glue connection mendukung referensi ke secret di AWS Secrets Manager, sehingga username dan password tidak disimpan di properti koneksi dan tidak terlihat di console. Glue mengambil secret saat runtime dengan role job, yang cukup diberi secretsmanager:GetSecretValue (dan kms:Decrypt bila memakai customer managed key) pada secret tersebut. Job script tidak perlu diubah karena koneksi yang sama tetap dipakai. Job parameter terlihat di konfigurasi dan log run. Parameter String tidak dienkripsi dan butuh perubahan kode. File teks di S3 menambah risiko dan tidak terintegrasi dengan koneksi. Aturan umum: credential untuk Glue connection → simpan di Secrets Manager dan referensikan dari connection.","r":["Salah — Job parameter dapat terlihat oleh siapa pun yang dapat melihat konfigurasi atau riwayat run.","Salah — Tipe String tidak terenkripsi dan mengharuskan perubahan pada setiap script.","Benar — Glue connection mendukung Secrets Manager secara native sehingga credential tersembunyi tanpa mengubah script.","Salah — File teks di S3 bukan penyimpanan secret yang aman dan tidak terintegrasi dengan Glue connection."],"k":"Tips ujian: credential di Glue connection → AWS Secrets Manager secret + GetSecretValue pada job role."},{"id":"E1B-68","d":1,"ts":"1.2.10","t":"Orchestrating LLM processing with Step Functions","q":"A data engineer is building a daily pipeline that runs an AWS Glue job to clean support ticket data, then sends each ticket's text to a foundation model on Amazon Bedrock to extract the product name and issue type, and finally writes the results to Amazon S3. The pipeline must retry failed model calls with backoff and must be easy to monitor visually. The engineer wants the LEAST custom code. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate the Glue job and call Amazon Bedrock through the Step Functions optimized integration, with a Map state, Retry policies, and an S3 output step.","Write a single Python script on an Amazon EC2 instance that runs the Glue job through the API and calls Bedrock in a loop with custom retry logic.","Use Amazon SQS to queue the tickets and a cron job on Amazon EC2 to call Bedrock.","Use Amazon EventBridge Scheduler to invoke the Bedrock model directly once per day for all tickets in a single request."],"a":[0],"e":"Penentunya adalah alur multi-langkah (Glue job → pemanggilan model per tiket → tulis ke S3), kebutuhan 'retry failed model calls with backoff', 'easy to monitor visually', dan 'LEAST custom code'. AWS Step Functions memiliki integrasi teroptimasi untuk menjalankan Glue job dan memanggil Amazon Bedrock (InvokeModel), Map state untuk memproses banyak item secara paralel, serta kebijakan Retry dengan backoff yang dideklarasikan tanpa kode; konsolnya menampilkan eksekusi secara visual. Skrip Python di EC2 adalah distraktor terdekat, tetapi menuntut kode retry, orkestrasi, dan pengelolaan server sendiri. SQS + cron di EC2 juga membutuhkan server dan logika kustom. Satu request untuk semua tiket akan melampaui batas konteks model dan tidak memberi retry per tiket. Aturan umum: orkestrasi ETL + LLM dengan retry dan visibilitas → Step Functions dengan integrasi Bedrock.","r":["Benar — Step Functions mengorkestrasi Glue dan Bedrock dengan integrasi bawaan, Map state, Retry, dan monitoring visual.","Salah — Membutuhkan banyak kode kustom dan pengelolaan EC2.","Salah — Cron di EC2 menambah server dan logika kustom tanpa monitoring alur visual.","Salah — Satu request untuk semua tiket melampaui batas konteks dan tidak dapat di-retry per tiket."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'orchestrate ETL steps + Bedrock calls with retries, visual monitoring' → Step Functions (Bedrock optimized integration)."},{"id":"E1A-11","d":1,"ts":"1.1.2","t":"Amazon AppFlow","q":"A sales operations team needs opportunity and account records from Salesforce copied to Amazon S3 once per day for analysis. The team has no developers and wants a managed, no-code solution that handles authentication and pagination of the Salesforce API. Which service should the team use?","o":["AWS Glue ETL job with a custom JDBC driver","AWS Transfer Family","AWS DataSync","Amazon AppFlow"],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: sumber SaaS 'Salesforce', 'no developers', 'no-code', dan 'handles authentication and pagination'. Amazon AppFlow adalah layanan integrasi SaaS yang fully managed dengan connector bawaan untuk Salesforce, menangani OAuth, pagination, dan batas API, serta bisa dijadwalkan harian dengan tujuan S3. Distraktor terdekat adalah Glue ETL dengan driver kustom: secara teknis mungkin, tetapi memerlukan kode dan pengelolaan driver. DataSync memindahkan file dari storage (NFS, SMB, HDFS, object storage), bukan data dari API SaaS. Transfer Family menerima file melalui SFTP/FTPS/FTP/AS2. Aturan umum: SaaS (Salesforce, ServiceNow, Zendesk, Google Analytics, dll.) ke AWS tanpa kode = Amazon AppFlow.","r":["Salah — Memerlukan pengembangan kode dan pengelolaan driver, bertentangan dengan no-code.","Salah — Transfer Family adalah layanan transfer file SFTP/FTPS/FTP/AS2, bukan connector SaaS.","Salah — DataSync memindahkan file dari sistem storage, bukan data dari API SaaS.","Benar — AppFlow memiliki connector Salesforce yang managed, menangani autentikasi dan pagination, dan bisa dijadwalkan."],"k":"SaaS → S3/Redshift tanpa kode → Amazon AppFlow."},{"id":"E3B-23","d":3,"ts":"3.3.7","t":"CloudWatch agent configuration","q":"A company runs a custom data ingestion application on 120 Amazon EC2 instances. The application writes logs to /var/log/ingest/*.log. A data engineer must send these logs to CloudWatch Logs and manage the logging configuration centrally so that changes can be rolled out to all instances automatically. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Write a cron script on each instance that calls the PutLogEvents API with the AWS CLI.","Install the Kinesis Agent on each instance and send the files to Amazon Data Firehose with an S3 destination.","Install the unified CloudWatch agent through AWS Systems Manager, store the agent configuration in Systems Manager Parameter Store, and use Systems Manager to apply the configuration to all instances.","Enable VPC Flow Logs for the subnet that contains the instances."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'send these logs to CloudWatch Logs', 'manage centrally', dan 'rolled out automatically'. Unified CloudWatch agent membaca file log lokal dan mengirimkannya ke log group, sedangkan konfigurasinya dapat disimpan di Systems Manager Parameter Store dan didistribusikan ke seluruh fleet dengan Systems Manager (Run Command atau State Manager). Distraktor terdekat adalah Kinesis Agent ke Firehose: mengirim data ke S3, bukan ke CloudWatch Logs, sehingga tidak memenuhi persyaratan. Cron script dengan PutLogEvents rapuh dan sulit dirawat di 120 instance. VPC Flow Logs mencatat traffic jaringan, bukan log aplikasi. Aturan: log file EC2/on-premises → CloudWatch agent + konfigurasi di Parameter Store.","r":["Salah — Script kustom di setiap instance sulit dirawat dan rawan error.","Salah — Tujuannya S3 melalui Firehose, bukan CloudWatch Logs.","Benar — CloudWatch agent dengan konfigurasi terpusat di Parameter Store dan distribusi lewat Systems Manager meminimalkan overhead.","Salah — VPC Flow Logs hanya mencatat metadata traffic jaringan."],"k":"Tips ujian: log aplikasi di EC2 → unified CloudWatch agent; konfigurasi terpusat → SSM Parameter Store."},{"id":"E2B-11","d":2,"ts":"2.2.3","t":"Glue crawler JDBC include path","q":"A company has an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database in private subnets with 40 schemas. The data engineering team wants the AWS Glue Data Catalog to contain table definitions only for the tables in the 'billing' schema so that AWS Glue ETL jobs can reference them. New tables are added to the schema every few weeks. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Export the schema DDL from PostgreSQL each week and create the Data Catalog tables with the AWS Glue CreateTable API.","Create an AWS Glue JDBC connection to the database and a crawler that uses the connection with the include path 'dbname/billing/%', scheduled to run weekly.","Use AWS DMS to copy the billing schema to Amazon S3 every week and run a crawler on the S3 output.","Create an Amazon Athena federated query connector for PostgreSQL and run SHOW TABLES each week."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'definitions only for the tables in the billing schema', 'new tables are added every few weeks' dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Glue crawler bisa meng-crawl sumber JDBC melalui Glue connection; include path berformat database/schema/table dengan wildcard % membatasi crawler ke skema billing saja. Dengan jadwal mingguan, tabel baru otomatis masuk ke Data Catalog tanpa script. DMS ke S3 lalu crawl menyalin data dan menghasilkan tabel S3, bukan definisi tabel sumber, jadi menambah biaya dan pipeline. Ekspor DDL manual dan Athena SHOW TABLES tidak mengisi Data Catalog secara otomatis. Ingat: discover skema database relasional ke Data Catalog → crawler + JDBC connection + include path.","r":["Salah — Ekspor DDL dan pemanggilan API manual adalah overhead kustom yang mudah tertinggal dari perubahan.","Benar — Crawler dengan JDBC connection dan include path 'dbname/billing/%' mengisi catalog otomatis hanya untuk skema billing.","Salah — DMS menyalin data ke S3 dan menghasilkan tabel berbeda; biaya dan kompleksitasnya tidak perlu.","Salah — Federated query untuk query lintas sumber, bukan untuk membuat definisi tabel di Data Catalog bagi Glue ETL."],"k":"Tips ujian: crawl database (JDBC) hanya sebagian skema → include path 'database/schema/%'."},{"id":"E1B-46","d":1,"ts":"1.2.7","t":"Small files problem in AWS Glue","q":"An AWS Glue Spark job uses a Spark DataFrame reader (spark.read.json) to read an S3 prefix that contains about 3 million small JSON files of 10 KB to 50 KB each. The job fails with an out-of-memory error on the driver while listing and planning the input, before any transformation runs. Which solution will resolve the issue with the LEAST code change?","o":["Increase the number of G.1X workers from 10 to 100.","Read the input with an AWS Glue DynamicFrame (create_dynamic_frame.from_options) and set groupFiles to inPartition with an appropriate groupSize so that many small files are read as larger groups.","Convert the job to a Glue Python shell job.","Enable job bookmarks so that the files are processed only once."],"a":[1],"e":"Gejala kuncinya adalah 'about 3 million small JSON files' dan OOM pada 'driver' saat listing dan perencanaan sebelum transformasi berjalan. Ketika setiap file kecil menjadi satu task/partition, driver harus melacak jutaan objek sehingga memorinya habis. Fitur grouping Glue pada DynamicFrame (groupFiles = inPartition dengan groupSize) membuat Glue membaca banyak file kecil sebagai satu kelompok, mengurangi jumlah task dan beban metadata pada driver; untuk DynamicFrame, Glue bahkan mengaktifkan grouping secara otomatis jika jumlah file input lebih dari 50.000, sedangkan reader DataFrame Spark biasa tidak memiliki fitur ini. Menambah worker adalah distraktor terdekat, tetapi masalah ada di driver, bukan executor, sehingga worker tambahan tidak membantu. Python shell tidak mampu memproses volume ini secara terdistribusi, dan bookmark tidak mengurangi jumlah file pada run pertama. Aturan umum: Glue lambat/OOM karena banyak small files → grouping (groupFiles/groupSize), dan perbaiki di hulu dengan compaction.","r":["Salah — OOM terjadi pada driver; menambah worker tidak mengurangi beban perencanaan driver.","Benar — DynamicFrame dengan grouping membaca banyak file kecil sebagai kelompok sehingga jumlah task dan beban memori driver berkurang, dengan perubahan kode kecil pada langkah baca.","Salah — Python shell tidak terdistribusi dan tidak cocok untuk jutaan file.","Salah — Bookmark tidak mengurangi jumlah file yang harus dibaca pada run pertama."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'millions of small files + driver OOM in Glue' → baca dengan DynamicFrame + grouping (groupFiles/groupSize; otomatis di atas 50.000 file), dan lakukan compaction di hulu."},{"id":"E1C-11","d":1,"ts":"1.3.1","t":"MWAA vs Step Functions selection","q":"A data platform team must choose an orchestrator for a new pipeline with about 40 interdependent tasks across Amazon EMR, AWS Glue, Amazon Redshift, and an on-premises database. The team writes all workflow logic in Python, needs to backfill the pipeline for the past 2 years of daily partitions, and wants an open source workflow definition that can be ported to other environments. Which service BEST meets these requirements?","o":["AWS Step Functions Express workflows","AWS Glue workflows","Amazon EventBridge Scheduler with one schedule for each task","Amazon Managed Workflows for Apache Airflow (Amazon MWAA)"],"a":[3],"e":"Kebutuhan pembedanya adalah 'Python', 'backfill ... past 2 years of daily partitions', dan 'open source workflow definition'. Amazon MWAA menjalankan Apache Airflow, yang mendefinisikan DAG dalam Python, mendukung catchup/backfill berdasarkan logical date, punya operator untuk EMR, Glue, Redshift, dan database lain, serta portabel karena open source. Distractor terdekat adalah Step Functions: sangat baik untuk orkestrasi serverless, tetapi definisinya Amazon States Language (bukan Python open source), tidak punya fitur backfill bawaan, dan Express dibatasi 5 menit. Glue workflows hanya untuk job dan crawler Glue. EventBridge Scheduler tidak mengelola dependensi antar task. Aturan umum: 'Python DAG', 'backfill', 'open source/portable', 'existing Airflow' → MWAA.","r":["Salah — Express workflows maksimum 5 menit, definisi dalam ASL, dan tidak ada backfill bawaan.","Salah — Glue workflows terbatas pada job, crawler, dan trigger Glue.","Salah — Jadwal terpisah tidak memodelkan dependensi antar 40 task.","Benar — Airflow di MWAA memakai DAG Python open source, mendukung backfill/catchup, dan punya operator untuk banyak sistem."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'backfill' + 'Python DAG' + 'open source' → MWAA; 'serverless, AWS-native, visual' → Step Functions."},{"id":"E1B-70","d":1,"ts":"1.2.10","t":"Calling Amazon Bedrock from data pipelines","q":"A company processes support tickets with an event-driven pipeline: each new ticket in Amazon S3 triggers an AWS Lambda function. The company now wants the function to extract named entities (customer name, product, and order number) from the free-text ticket body by using a large language model. The company has no ML infrastructure and wants the LEAST operational overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Host an open-source LLM on Amazon EC2 GPU instances and call it from the Lambda function.","Deploy a model to an Amazon SageMaker AI real-time endpoint and manage endpoint scaling for the Lambda traffic.","Index the tickets in Amazon Kendra and query the index from the Lambda function to retrieve entities.","Call a foundation model through the Amazon Bedrock Converse or InvokeModel API from the Lambda function, with an IAM role that allows bedrock:InvokeModel."],"a":[3],"e":"Penentunya adalah 'no ML infrastructure', kebutuhan ekstraksi entitas dengan 'large language model' dari teks bebas, dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Amazon Bedrock menyediakan foundation model melalui API serverless (Converse atau InvokeModel), sehingga fungsi Lambda cukup memanggil API dengan izin IAM yang sesuai tanpa mengelola server, GPU, atau endpoint. Endpoint SageMaker AI adalah distraktor terdekat, tetapi Anda harus men-deploy model, memilih instance, dan mengelola scaling endpoint. Hosting LLM di EC2 GPU memiliki overhead tertinggi. Amazon Kendra adalah layanan pencarian enterprise (dan kini dalam mode maintenance), bukan alat ekstraksi entitas berbasis LLM. Aturan umum: menambahkan LLM ke pipeline data tanpa infrastruktur → panggil Amazon Bedrock API dari Lambda, Glue, atau Step Functions.","r":["Salah — Mengelola instance GPU dan server model menambah overhead terbesar.","Salah — Endpoint SageMaker AI membutuhkan deployment model dan pengelolaan kapasitas.","Salah — Kendra adalah layanan pencarian, bukan ekstraksi entitas dengan LLM.","Benar — Bedrock adalah API serverless sehingga Lambda dapat memanggil LLM tanpa infrastruktur ML."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'add LLM to pipeline, no ML infrastructure' → Amazon Bedrock API (serverless), bukan self-hosted model."},{"id":"E1A-70","d":1,"ts":"1.1.12","t":"Stateful vs stateless transactions","q":"A data engineer is classifying the operations in a new streaming pipeline as stateless or stateful in order to choose the right processing services. Which TWO operations are stateful? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Masking the credit card number field in each record.","Removing duplicate events that have the same event ID within a 10-minute period.","Converting each JSON record to a different schema.","Dropping records whose status field equals 'test'.","Grouping a user's clicks into sessions that end after 30 minutes of inactivity."],"a":[1,4],"e":"Kata kunci adalah definisi 'stateless' vs 'stateful'. Operasi stateless memproses setiap record secara independen tanpa mengingat record lain, misalnya masking field, konversi skema per record, atau filter berdasarkan nilai field. Operasi stateful memerlukan informasi dari record sebelumnya atau berikutnya: deduplikasi dalam periode waktu harus mengingat event ID yang sudah terlihat, dan sessionization harus mengingat aktivitas terakhir per user untuk menentukan kapan sesi berakhir. Distraktor terdekat adalah filter status = 'test': terlihat seperti logika bisnis, tetapi keputusan hanya bergantung pada record itu sendiri. Implikasinya: operasi stateless cocok untuk Lambda atau transformasi Firehose dan mudah di-scale, sedangkan operasi stateful membutuhkan state store tahan lama dan checkpoint (misalnya Flink, Glue streaming dengan checkpoint, atau KCL dengan lease table DynamoDB). Aturan umum: butuh mengingat record lain atau waktu = stateful.","r":["Salah — Masking field hanya bergantung pada record itu sendiri (stateless).","Benar — Deduplikasi harus mengingat event ID yang sudah terlihat selama periode tertentu.","Salah — Konversi skema per record bersifat stateless.","Salah — Filter berdasarkan nilai field dalam record yang sama bersifat stateless.","Benar — Sessionization harus mengingat aktivitas terakhir per user untuk menutup sesi."],"k":"Stateful = butuh mengingat record lain (dedup, session, window, join); stateless = per record (mask, filter, convert)."},{"id":"E1C-35","d":1,"ts":"1.3.4","t":"Failure alerts with EventBridge and SNS","q":"A data engineer must notify the data operations team by email whenever any of the company's AWS Glue jobs fails. The solution must be event-driven and use the LEAST operational overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches 'Glue Job State Change' events with state FAILED and targets an Amazon SNS topic that has email subscriptions for the team.","Create a CloudWatch Logs subscription filter on every Glue job log group that invokes a Lambda function to send email through Amazon SES.","Schedule a Lambda function every 10 minutes that lists failed job runs and publishes to Amazon SNS.","Add code to the end of every Glue script that sends an email if an exception occurs."],"a":[0],"e":"Kebutuhan: email saat 'any of the company's AWS Glue jobs fails', 'event-driven', dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Glue mengirim event 'Glue Job State Change' ke EventBridge; satu rule dengan filter state FAILED yang menargetkan topik SNS dengan langganan email langsung memenuhi semuanya tanpa kode. Distractor terdekat adalah subscription filter log + Lambda + SES: perlu dibuat per log group, menulis kode, dan mencocokkan teks log yang tidak selalu mencerminkan status job. Lambda terjadwal adalah polling, bukan event-driven. Kode notifikasi di dalam script tidak menangkap kegagalan seperti timeout atau gagal start, dan harus diulang di setiap job. Aturan umum: notifikasi perubahan status layanan AWS → EventBridge rule → SNS.","r":["Benar — EventBridge menangkap status FAILED untuk semua job dan SNS mengirim email tanpa kode.","Salah — Kode kustom per log group dan pencocokan teks log menambah overhead.","Salah — Polling terjadwal tidak event-driven dan menambah latensi.","Salah — Tidak menangkap timeout atau kegagalan sebelum script berjalan, dan harus diulang di setiap job."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'alert when Glue job fails' → EventBridge rule (Glue Job State Change) → SNS."},{"id":"E4B-59","d":4,"ts":"4.5.7","t":"Third-party data sharing with AWS Data Exchange","q":"A weather analytics company wants to license its curated datasets to external customers in other AWS accounts. Customers must be able to discover the products, accept subscription terms, and be billed through AWS, and the company wants to deliver new data revisions automatically to subscribers. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Generate Amazon S3 presigned URLs for each customer and send invoices from the company's billing system.","Use AWS Lake Formation cross-account grants for each customer account.","Publish the datasets as data products on AWS Data Exchange with subscription terms and pricing.","Create a Redshift datashare for each customer and track usage manually for billing."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: berbagi ke 'external customers', 'discover the products', 'accept subscription terms', 'billed through AWS', dan 'deliver new data revisions automatically'. AWS Data Exchange adalah pola berbagi data dengan pihak ketiga: penyedia mempublikasikan data product dengan harga dan subscription terms, pelanggan menemukannya, berlangganan dan ditagih melalui AWS, dan revisi baru otomatis tersedia bagi subscriber (Data Exchange juga mendukung pengiriman melalui S3, Redshift datashare, API, dan Lake Formation). Distraktor terdekat adalah Lake Formation cross-account grant: cocok untuk berbagi internal antar akun yang dipercaya, tetapi tidak menyediakan katalog publik, terms, maupun billing. Redshift datashare per pelanggan dengan billing manual menambah overhead. Presigned URL tidak memiliki discovery, terms, revisi otomatis, maupun billing terintegrasi. Aturan umum: berbagi/menjual data ke pihak eksternal dengan lisensi dan billing → AWS Data Exchange; berbagi internal → Lake Formation/Redshift data sharing/SageMaker Catalog.","r":["Salah — Presigned URL tidak menyediakan discovery, terms, revisi otomatis, atau billing AWS.","Salah — Lake Formation cocok untuk sharing internal, tanpa marketplace, terms, atau billing.","Benar — Data Exchange menyediakan discovery, subscription terms, billing AWS, dan pengiriman revisi otomatis.","Salah — Datashare per pelanggan dengan penagihan manual menambah overhead operasional."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'license/sell data to external customers, billing via AWS' → AWS Data Exchange."},{"id":"E2C-46","d":2,"ts":"2.4.6","t":"Embeddings model consistency","q":"A company has an Amazon Bedrock knowledge base that was built with Embeddings Model A. A newer embeddings model, Model B, gives better retrieval quality in testing. The data engineer wants to switch the knowledge base to Model B. What must happen to the existing vectors?","o":["Nothing; vectors from Model A and Model B can be compared directly in the same index.","Only new documents need to be embedded with Model B; old vectors remain valid.","All documents must be re-embedded with Model B into a vector index configured for Model B, because vectors from different embeddings models are not comparable.","The existing vectors can be converted to Model B by multiplying them by a fixed scaling factor."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah mengganti embeddings model pada knowledge base yang sudah berisi vektor. Setiap embeddings model menghasilkan ruang vektor sendiri (dengan dimensi dan makna koordinat yang berbeda), sehingga vektor dari Model A tidak dapat dibandingkan secara bermakna dengan vektor query dari Model B. Karena itu seluruh dokumen harus di-embed ulang dengan Model B ke index yang dikonfigurasi untuk dimensi Model B, biasanya dengan membuat knowledge base atau index baru lalu melakukan ingestion penuh. Mencampur vektor lama dan baru menghasilkan similarity score yang tidak berarti. Tidak ada faktor skala sederhana untuk mengonversi antar ruang embedding. Aturan umum: ganti embeddings model → re-embed semua data; query dan dokumen harus memakai model yang sama.","r":["Salah — Ruang vektor setiap model berbeda sehingga perbandingan langsung tidak bermakna.","Salah — Vektor lama dari Model A tidak kompatibel dengan query yang di-embed dengan Model B.","Benar — Semua dokumen harus di-embed ulang dengan Model B ke index yang sesuai.","Salah — Tidak ada transformasi skala sederhana antar ruang embedding model yang berbeda."],"k":"Tips ujian: ganti embeddings model → re-embed seluruh corpus; query & dokumen wajib model yang sama."},{"id":"E3A-70","d":3,"ts":"3.2.3","t":"Athena views","q":"Analysts in several teams repeatedly write the same complex Amazon Athena query that joins three tables in the AWS Glue Data Catalog, casts several columns, and excludes internal columns. The data engineer wants to give them a simple, reusable object that always reflects the latest data in Amazon S3, does not store a second copy of the data, and exposes only the approved columns. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Run a CREATE TABLE AS SELECT (CTAS) statement every morning to materialize the joined result.","Run an UNLOAD statement to export the joined result to a shared S3 prefix.","Run an AWS Glue crawler on the S3 locations of the three tables to create a combined table.","Create an Athena view with CREATE VIEW that contains the join, casts, and approved column list, and have analysts query the view."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'reusable object', 'always reflects the latest data', 'does not store a second copy', dan 'exposes only approved columns'. View di Athena (CREATE VIEW) adalah query tersimpan yang terdaftar di Glue Data Catalog; setiap kali view di-query, Athena menjalankan query dasarnya atas data terbaru di S3, tanpa menyimpan salinan data. View menyembunyikan kompleksitas join dan cast serta hanya menampilkan kolom yang disetujui. CTAS dan UNLOAD menulis salinan data baru ke S3 yang menjadi basi sampai dijalankan ulang. Crawler hanya menyimpulkan skema dari file dan tidak bisa membuat hasil join dari tiga tabel. Perlu diingat bahwa view Athena tidak menambah performa karena query dasar tetap dijalankan setiap kali. Aturan umum: abstraksi logis tanpa salinan data → view; hasil yang dimaterialisasi untuk performa → CTAS (Athena) atau materialized view (Redshift).","r":["Salah — CTAS menyimpan salinan data yang basi sampai dijalankan ulang.","Salah — UNLOAD mengekspor salinan data dan tidak selalu mencerminkan data terbaru.","Salah — Crawler hanya membuat tabel dari skema file, bukan hasil join tiga tabel.","Benar — View Athena menyimpan definisi query, selalu membaca data terbaru, dan hanya menampilkan kolom yang disetujui."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'reusable, always current, no data copy' → CREATE VIEW; 'materialize result as new table' → CTAS."},{"id":"E1B-35","d":1,"ts":"1.2.4","t":"EMR auto-termination","q":"A data team launches an Amazon EMR on EC2 cluster for interactive and scheduled Spark work. The cluster often remains running for many hours after the last job completes because users forget to terminate it. The team wants to stop paying for idle clusters with the LEAST operational overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create an AWS Lambda function that checks the cluster every hour and terminates it if the CPU utilization is low.","Ask users to terminate the cluster manually and send a weekly cost report.","Configure an EMR auto-termination policy with an idle timeout on the cluster.","Convert all core nodes to Spot Instances."],"a":[2],"e":"Penentunya adalah cluster yang 'remains running for many hours after the last job completes' dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. EMR menyediakan auto-termination policy bawaan: cluster otomatis dihentikan setelah tidak aktif selama durasi idle timeout yang ditentukan. Lambda kustom yang memeriksa CPU adalah distraktor terdekat karena bisa bekerja, tetapi Anda harus menulis, menguji, dan memelihara logikanya, dan CPU rendah bukan indikator idle yang andal. Mengandalkan pengguna menghentikan cluster secara manual terbukti gagal. Spot pada core node menurunkan harga per jam, tetapi tetap membayar cluster yang menganggur dan menambah risiko kehilangan data HDFS. Aturan umum: hindari biaya cluster EMR idle → auto-termination policy, cluster transient, atau EMR Serverless.","r":["Salah — Solusi kustom menambah beban pemeliharaan dan CPU bukan ukuran idle yang andal.","Salah — Proses manual tidak menjamin cluster dihentikan.","Benar — Auto-termination bawaan menghentikan cluster idle secara otomatis tanpa kode kustom.","Salah — Masih membayar cluster idle dan berisiko pada data HDFS di core node."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'EMR cluster left idle' → auto-termination policy (idle timeout) atau transient cluster/EMR Serverless."},{"id":"E3B-48","d":3,"ts":"3.4.2","t":"Glue Data Quality rule recommendations","q":"A company has 300 tables in the AWS Glue Data Catalog and no data quality rules yet. A data engineer must establish a baseline of data quality rules for every table quickly, without manually analyzing each table's columns, and then refine the rules over time. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST effort?","o":["Manually write DQDL rules for each table after querying every column with Amazon Athena.","Use AWS Glue Data Quality rule recommendations on the Data Catalog tables to generate DQDL rulesets, then review and edit them.","Create one DataBrew project per table and inspect the sample data visually.","Deploy open source Great Expectations on Amazon EC2 and write expectation suites by hand."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'establish a baseline quickly', '300 tables', dan 'without manually analyzing each column'. AWS Glue Data Quality dapat menghasilkan rule recommendations untuk tabel Data Catalog: layanan menganalisis data (statistik kolom seperti completeness, uniqueness, rentang nilai) dan menghasilkan ruleset DQDL awal yang dapat direview dan diedit. Distraktor terdekat adalah menulis DQDL manual setelah query Athena — memenuhi hasil, tetapi sangat lambat untuk 300 tabel. Satu project DataBrew per tabel juga manual. Great Expectations di EC2 menambah infrastruktur dan penulisan aturan manual. Aturan: 'start quickly with suggested rules' → Glue Data Quality recommendations.","r":["Salah — Analisis manual 300 tabel memakan banyak waktu.","Benar — Rule recommendations menganalisis data dan menghasilkan ruleset DQDL awal secara otomatis.","Salah — Inspeksi visual per tabel tetap manual dan tidak menghasilkan aturan otomatis.","Salah — Menambah server yang harus dikelola dan aturan masih ditulis manual."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'generate/recommend data quality rules automatically' → Glue Data Quality rule recommendations."},{"id":"E3B-59","d":3,"ts":"3.4.4","t":"DataBrew sampling","q":"A data analyst creates an AWS Glue DataBrew project on a 400 GB log dataset in Amazon S3 that is sorted by event time. The project uses the default sample of the first rows. The analyst sees no invalid values, but the downstream team reports many malformed records generated in the last two weeks, which appear at the end of the dataset. What should the analyst change to make the interactive sample more representative?","o":["Increase the size of the project session.","Run a DataBrew recipe job on the full dataset before looking at the project.","Switch the dataset to Apache Parquet format.","Change the project's sampling type to random rows so that records are drawn from across the whole dataset."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'dataset sorted by event time', 'default sample of the first rows', dan record bermasalah ada 'at the end of the dataset'. DataBrew project bekerja pada sampel (default: first n rows); jika data terurut, sampel 'first n' hanya mewakili data paling awal dan melewatkan masalah terbaru. Mengubah tipe sampel menjadi random rows mengambil baris acak dari seluruh dataset sehingga lebih representatif (alternatifnya last n rows bila fokus pada data terbaru). Distraktor terdekat adalah menjalankan recipe job pada data penuh: recipe job menulis output transformasi, bukan memperbaiki sampel interaktif untuk eksplorasi. Format Parquet tidak mengubah strategi sampling. Aturan: sampel 'first n' dari data terurut menimbulkan bias → gunakan random sampling.","r":["Salah — Ukuran sesi tidak mengubah baris mana yang diambil sebagai sampel.","Salah — Recipe job menjalankan transformasi dan tidak mengubah sampel yang dilihat di project.","Salah — Format file tidak memengaruhi bias sampel 'first n rows'.","Benar — Sampel acak mengambil baris dari seluruh dataset sehingga masalah di bagian akhir ikut terwakili."],"k":"Tips ujian: sampel 'first n rows' pada data terurut = bias → random sample."},{"id":"E4B-24","d":4,"ts":"4.4.1","t":"CloudTrail data events for S3","q":"A company stores sensitive customer documents in an Amazon S3 bucket. Auditors require a record of every IAM principal that reads or deletes individual objects in that bucket. The company already has a CloudTrail trail that logs management events. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Use the CloudTrail event history, because it already records all S3 API calls.","Enable Amazon S3 Storage Lens advanced metrics on the bucket.","Enable CloudTrail data events for Amazon S3 on the existing trail, scoped to the sensitive bucket, for read and write events.","Enable AWS Config recording for the bucket."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci adalah akses ke 'individual objects' (GetObject, DeleteObject). Operasi tingkat objek di S3 adalah data events, yang secara default tidak dicatat oleh CloudTrail dan tidak muncul di event history; hanya management events seperti CreateBucket atau PutBucketPolicy yang tercatat otomatis. Mengaktifkan S3 data events pada trail, dengan advanced event selector yang membatasi ke bucket sensitif, mencatat siapa yang membaca dan menghapus objek sekaligus menekan biaya. Distraktor terdekat adalah event history: hanya berisi management events. Storage Lens memberi metrik penggunaan dan aktivitas agregat, bukan identitas per request. Config merekam konfigurasi bucket, bukan akses ke objek. Aturan umum: audit akses objek S3 → CloudTrail data events (biaya tambahan, batasi ke bucket yang perlu).","r":["Salah — Event history hanya berisi management events, bukan operasi objek seperti GetObject.","Salah — Storage Lens memberikan metrik agregat tanpa identitas principal per request.","Benar — S3 data events pada trail mencatat setiap operasi baca/hapus objek beserta identitas pemanggil.","Salah — Config melacak konfigurasi resource, bukan akses terhadap objek."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'who read/deleted S3 objects' → CloudTrail data events (tidak aktif default)."},{"id":"E4A-13","d":4,"ts":"4.1.4","t":"Lambda execution role","q":"An AWS Lambda function processes files that land in an Amazon S3 bucket and writes the results to an Amazon DynamoDB table. A developer currently stores an IAM user's access key and secret key in the function's environment variables. The security team wants to remove long-term credentials from the function. Which solution meets this requirement?","o":["Create an IAM role that trusts lambda.amazonaws.com with permissions to read the bucket and write to the table, and set it as the function's execution role.","Move the access key and secret key to AWS Secrets Manager and retrieve them in the function code at startup.","Add a resource-based policy to the Lambda function that allows the function to access Amazon S3 and DynamoDB.","Encrypt the environment variables with a customer managed AWS KMS key and rotate the access keys every 90 days."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'remove long-term credentials'. Lambda dirancang untuk memakai execution role: saat fungsi berjalan, Lambda meng-assume role tersebut dan SDK otomatis mendapat credential sementara yang dirotasi oleh AWS. Trust policy role harus mengizinkan lambda.amazonaws.com, dan permission policy-nya cukup berisi akses baca bucket dan tulis ke tabel. Menyimpan access key di Secrets Manager memang lebih aman daripada environment variable, tetapi tetap memakai credential jangka panjang. Resource-based policy pada Lambda mengatur siapa yang boleh memanggil fungsi, bukan apa yang boleh diakses fungsi. Enkripsi environment variable tidak menghilangkan access key. Aturan umum: compute di AWS (Lambda, EC2, Glue, ECS) mendapat permission lewat IAM role, bukan access key.","r":["Benar — Execution role memberi credential sementara otomatis tanpa access key jangka panjang.","Salah — Access key tetap merupakan credential jangka panjang walaupun disimpan di Secrets Manager.","Salah — Resource-based policy Lambda mengatur siapa yang boleh invoke fungsi, bukan akses fungsi ke service lain.","Salah — Enkripsi dan rotasi tetap mempertahankan credential jangka panjang di fungsi."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'remove access keys from Lambda/EC2' → IAM role (execution role/instance profile)."},{"id":"E1B-11","d":1,"ts":"1.2.1","t":"EMR on EKS","q":"A company already runs a large Amazon EKS cluster for its microservices, and the cluster has significant unused capacity at night. The data team wants to run nightly Apache Spark transformation jobs on the same infrastructure to improve resource utilization, while still using an AWS-optimized Spark runtime and job-level monitoring. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create a separate Amazon EMR on EC2 cluster that runs only at night.","Run the Spark jobs as AWS Glue ETL jobs with the Flex execution class.","Install open-source Spark on Amazon ECS tasks that run on AWS Fargate.","Use Amazon EMR on EKS to submit the Spark jobs to a namespace on the existing EKS cluster."],"a":[3],"e":"Frasa penentu adalah 'already runs a large Amazon EKS cluster', 'unused capacity', 'same infrastructure', dan 'AWS-optimized Spark runtime'. Amazon EMR on EKS memungkinkan job Spark dikirim ke namespace (virtual cluster) di cluster EKS yang sudah ada, memakai runtime EMR yang dioptimalkan, dan berbagi kapasitas node dengan aplikasi lain sehingga utilisasi meningkat. Cluster EMR on EC2 terpisah adalah distraktor terdekat karena berjalan dengan baik, tetapi menambah infrastruktur baru dan tidak memanfaatkan kapasitas EKS yang menganggur. Glue Flex murah tetapi berjalan di kapasitas Glue, bukan di cluster EKS milik perusahaan. Spark open-source di ECS Fargate tidak memakai runtime EMR dan menuntut banyak konfigurasi manual. Aturan umum: sudah punya Kubernetes/EKS dan ingin Spark di sana → EMR on EKS.","r":["Salah — Menambah cluster baru dan tidak memanfaatkan kapasitas EKS yang tidak terpakai.","Salah — Glue Flex berjalan di infrastruktur terkelola Glue, bukan di cluster EKS yang ada.","Salah — Spark open-source di Fargate tidak memakai runtime EMR yang dioptimalkan dan membutuhkan pengaturan manual yang rumit.","Benar — EMR on EKS menjalankan Spark dengan runtime EMR pada cluster EKS yang sudah ada sehingga utilisasi meningkat."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'existing EKS cluster + Spark + shared infrastructure' → Amazon EMR on EKS."},{"id":"E4B-12","d":4,"ts":"4.3.2","t":"KMS envelope encryption","q":"An application running on Amazon EC2 must encrypt 500 MB files with an AWS KMS customer managed key before storing them in a third-party storage system. A developer tried to call the KMS Encrypt API directly on the file and received an error. Which approach should the data engineer recommend?","o":["Split each file into 4 KB chunks and call the KMS Encrypt API once for each chunk.","Create an asymmetric KMS key because asymmetric keys support larger payloads.","Call the KMS GenerateDataKey API, encrypt the file locally with the plaintext data key, store the encrypted data key with the file, and then discard the plaintext data key from memory.","Call GenerateDataKey and store the plaintext data key in AWS Secrets Manager so it can be reused to encrypt all future files."],"a":[2],"e":"Penyebab error: KMS Encrypt API hanya menerima plaintext hingga 4 KB, sehingga file 500 MB tidak bisa dienkripsi langsung oleh KMS. Pola yang benar adalah envelope encryption: GenerateDataKey mengembalikan data key dalam bentuk plaintext dan terenkripsi; aplikasi mengenkripsi file secara lokal dengan plaintext key, menyimpan encrypted data key bersama file, lalu menghapus plaintext key dari memori. Untuk dekripsi, aplikasi memanggil KMS Decrypt pada encrypted data key. Distraktor terdekat adalah memecah file menjadi potongan 4 KB: secara teori bisa, tetapi menghasilkan ratusan ribu panggilan API, lambat, mahal, dan rentan throttling. Kunci asimetris justru memiliki batas payload yang lebih kecil. Menyimpan plaintext data key di Secrets Manager untuk dipakai ulang melemahkan keamanan karena kunci data seharusnya tidak pernah disimpan dalam bentuk plaintext. Aturan umum: data besar + KMS → envelope encryption dengan GenerateDataKey (inilah yang dilakukan AWS Encryption SDK).","r":["Salah — Ratusan ribu panggilan Encrypt sangat lambat, mahal, dan rentan throttling.","Salah — Kunci asimetris KMS memiliki batas payload yang bahkan lebih kecil dan tidak cocok untuk file besar.","Benar — Envelope encryption dengan GenerateDataKey adalah pola standar untuk mengenkripsi data besar dengan KMS.","Salah — Menyimpan plaintext data key secara permanen melanggar prinsip envelope encryption dan memperbesar risiko kebocoran."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'encrypt data larger than 4 KB with KMS' → envelope encryption (GenerateDataKey, encrypt locally)."}]});